#: src/introduction.md:3
msgid ""
"**OpenCrabs** is a self-hosted, provider-agnostic AI orchestration agent "
"that runs as a single Rust binary. It automates your terminal, browser, "
"channels (Telegram/Discord/Slack/WhatsApp/Trello), and codebase, all while "
"respecting your privacy and keeping you in control."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:5
msgid ""
"**11,091 tests** across providers, tools, channels, TUI, self-healing, and "
"browser automation."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:7
msgid "What Makes OpenCrabs Different"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:9
msgid "Zero Telemetry, Not Even Opt-In"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:10
msgid ""
"**OpenCrabs does not phone home. Ever.** No analytics, no tracking, no usage "
"statistics, no remote logging, no crash reports"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:11
msgid ""
"Your conversations, tools, memory, configuration, and API keys never leave "
"your machine"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:12
msgid ""
"The only outbound traffic is what you explicitly initiate: LLM API calls, "
"web searches, GitHub commands, browser automation"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:13
msgid ""
"Not a privacy-policy checkbox: there is no telemetry code to disable, no "
"opt-out flag, no analytics service to block. There is simply nothing to send"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:15
msgid "Provider-Agnostic by Design"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:16
msgid ""
"**16 built-in providers + Custom OpenAI Compatible**: Anthropic Claude, "
"OpenAI, Gemini, Xiaomi MiMo, OpenRouter, Qwen (DashScope), MiniMax, Ollama, "
"z.ai GLM, GitHub Copilot, Codex, Codex CLI, OpenCode, OpenCode CLI, "
"**Moonshot AI (Kimi)**, Command Code CLI"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:17
msgid ""
"**Native CLI integration**: use Claude Code CLI, OpenCode CLI, Codex CLI, "
"and Command Code CLI as providers without API keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:18
msgid ""
"**Sticky fallback chain**: auto-failover on rate limits or errors, "
"health-aware persistence survives restarts"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:19
msgid ""
"**Prompt caching** across Anthropic, OpenRouter, Gemini, Qwen DashScope "
"reduces costs up to 95%"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:20
msgid ""
"**Context window override**: cap or expand context for any model via config "
"(the built-in OpenCrabs provider is the exception: its window is fixed at "
"200k)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:21
msgid ""
"**Xiaomi MiMo**: 30+ models including the MiMo reasoning series, keyed "
"provider"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:22
msgid ""
"**Moonshot AI (Kimi)**: API plan (api.moonshot.ai) and Coding plan "
"(api.kimi.com) endpoints, reasoning-effort config, plan-tier context window"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:25
msgid ""
"**Sessions are fully isolated agents**: each with its own brain, provider, "
"model, working directory, and history"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:26
msgid ""
"**Typed sub-agents**: `general`, `explore`, `plan`, `code`, `research` with "
"tailored tool access"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:27
msgid ""
"**Team orchestration**: `team_create`, `team_broadcast`, `team_delete` for "
"coordinated workflows"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:28
msgid ""
"**Per-call provider/model overrides**: mix models across teams (plan with "
"GLM, code with Deepseek, review with Kimi)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:29
msgid "**A2A protocol**: JSON-RPC 2.0 gateway for agent-to-agent communication"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:31
msgid "Channel-Native Communication"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid ""
"**Telegram, Discord, Slack, WhatsApp, Trello**, full bot integration with "
"DMs, groups, and threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:33
msgid ""
"**Telegram rich messages**: native tables, headings, lists, math via "
"`rich_messages` config"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"**Draft message streaming**: live \"typing...\" updates as tokens generate "
"in DMs"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:35
msgid "**Collapsible blocks**: `<details>/<summary>` sections for long outputs"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:36
msgid ""
"**Forum topic session isolation**: each topic in Telegram supergroups gets "
"its own session"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:37
msgid ""
"**Telegram reactions**: the bot reads inbound emoji reactions and can reply "
"with a reaction instead of a message when that fits"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:38
msgid ""
"**Frame reactions (v0.3.61)**: inbound reactions read by sentiment, agent "
"addresses user by first name"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:39
msgid ""
"**Mid-turn reactions (v0.3.61)**: a reaction during a running turn injects "
"into the current loop instead of firing a second turn"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:40
msgid ""
"**Follow-up suggestions (v0.3.69)**: tap-to-send optional follow-ups on "
"Telegram, Discord, Slack, WhatsApp; fill-not-submit in TUI"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:41
msgid ""
"**Telegram plan card re-stick (v0.3.71)**: re-stick plan card and fold prose "
"into it when buried"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:42
msgid ""
"**Full group history capture (v0.3.73)**: persist every group message to "
"history, even from non-allowlisted senders and bots"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:43
msgid ""
"**Correct group speaker (v0.3.73)**: stop addressing a group-history sender "
"as the current speaker"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:44
msgid ""
"**Session inheritance**: `/new` inherits the working directory from your "
"most recent session"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:45
msgid ""
"**`/goal` across all channels**: set autonomous goals from Telegram, "
"Discord, Slack, WhatsApp"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:46
msgid "**Voice support**: local Whisper STT + Piper TTS, fully offline"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:47
msgid ""
"**Cross-channel crash recovery**: pending requests route back to originating "
"channel on restart"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:48
msgid "**`/cowork`**: create shared workspaces from channels and TUI"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:49
msgid ""
"**`/rename`, `/profiles`, `/cd`**, manage sessions, profiles, and "
"directories from any channel"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:51
msgid "Self-Healing & Self-Improvement"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:52
msgid ""
"**Recursive Self-Improvement (RSI)**: agent analyzes performance, identifies "
"patterns, and rewrites brain files"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:53
msgid ""
"**Phantom tool call detection**: catches when the model narrates changes "
"without executing tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:54
msgid ""
"**Self-heal phantom detection (v0.3.72)**: catch zero-tool turns that claim "
"high-stakes side-effects (ship/push/tag/release)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:55
msgid ""
"**Config edits via config_manager only (v0.3.74)**: the agent never "
"raw-edits config.toml/keys.toml; every write is validated before it lands"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:56
msgid ""
"**Brain dedup (v0.3.75)**: `/dedup` command plus post-write and weekly "
"cross-file scans keep brain files from drifting into duplication, with "
"Telegram inline-keyboard approval"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:57
msgid ""
"**Brain-file hints on tool misses (v0.3.75)**: relevant brain notes surface "
"automatically when a tool call misses or errors"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:58
msgid ""
"**Proactive memory surfacing (v0.3.76)**: relevant memory surfaces without "
"being asked when conversation context matches stored knowledge"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:59
msgid ""
"**Natural model naming (v0.3.76)**: `/models opus` works; colloquial names "
"resolve to exact model IDs"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:60
msgid ""
"**Plan/execute provider routing (v0.3.76)**: route planning and execution "
"onto separate providers/models"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:61
msgid ""
"**Thinking-loop timeout (v0.3.78)**: catches infinite reasoning loops, fires "
"phantom enforcement with sticky fallback"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:62
msgid ""
"**Epistemic engine (v0.3.78)**: belief tracking with confidence levels, "
"OODA/BDI cognitive mesh, Orient gate before plan execution"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:63
msgid ""
"**Ralph verification gate (v0.3.78)**: criteria-aware task verification with "
"iteration cap; tasks must meet stated acceptance criteria"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:64
msgid ""
"**TOML safety gates (v0.3.78)**: runtime-configurable bash blocklist with "
"hot-reload, quoted-secret redaction, brain file verification"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:65
msgid ""
"**Mission Control analytics (v0.3.78)**: D/W/M filter, 3-across card grid, "
"phantom/model/streaming tabs, dedicated events DB"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:66
msgid ""
"**OpenAI TTS onboarding (v0.3.78)**: voice selector and API key field in the "
"onboarding wizard"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:67
msgid ""
"**Homebrew install (v0.3.79)**: `brew install opencrabs` from homebrew-core: "
"prebuilt binary, both architectures, no Rust toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:68
msgid ""
"**`/restart` and `/exit` (v0.3.79)**: restart or shut down from any channel "
"or the TUI; owner-only on channels, announce before acting"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:69
msgid ""
"**Quota circuit breaker (v0.3.79)**: quota-exhausted providers get a TTL "
"breaker and are skipped in fallback walks; chain exhaustion reported "
"explicitly"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:70
msgid ""
"**Plan state across sessions (v0.3.79)**: plans survive session boundaries; "
"isolated plan-task execution defaults on, Ralph verifies in the session's "
"own directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:71
msgid ""
"**Theme system (v0.5.0)**: verified presets, an interactive picker, and your "
"own themes from `~/.opencrabs/themes/*.toml`; truecolor is detected with an "
"ANSI-256 fallback tier, and a preset whose contrast would make text "
"unreadable is refused"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:72
msgid ""
"**Structural code memory (v0.5.0)**: tree-sitter builds a symbol and "
"call-graph index beside the text index, so \"who calls X\" walks real call "
"edges while conceptual questions keep the text lane (#1324)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:73
msgid ""
"**Drop transfer over SSH (v0.5.0)**: a file dropped into a TUI running on a "
"remote host is pulled back through the connection already open, with an "
"`opencrabs drop-agent` on the client side (#1289)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:74
msgid ""
"**Notify delivery verdicts (v0.5.0)**: `session_notify` returns a "
"machine-readable send result, depth-3 injection receipts make `notify_id` "
"checkable, and delivery redirects to the session that owns the channel now"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:75
msgid ""
"**Background compaction (v0.5.0)**: the summariser runs off the turn instead "
"of holding the session while it works"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:76
msgid ""
"**Token redaction at the writer (v0.5.0)**: a provider error carrying a URL "
"can no longer leak the bot token into a log, wherever it is logged from "
"(#1322)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:77
msgid ""
"**Receive-only Telegram userbot (v0.5.0, experimental)**: feature-gated "
"MTProto capture with local QR/code/2FA login; it stores allowlisted text for "
"retrieval and never acts as the user"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:78
msgid ""
"**Temporal grounding (v0.5.1)**: the agent always knows what time it is: "
"every turn carries a time-stamped marker in the user's timezone, and the "
"system prompt stays byte-stable for provider caching (#1516)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:79
msgid ""
"**Per-job cron sessions (v0.5.1)**: every scheduled job gets its own "
"session, so two jobs running at the same time can never bleed into each "
"other's context or providers (#1511)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:80
msgid ""
"**Skill-glob gating (v0.5.1)**: a skill's `globs:` list can refuse tool "
"calls that touch matching files until the agent has actually read the skill "
"body (#1515)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:81
msgid ""
"**Config writes validated against the struct (v0.5.1)**, the write guard and "
"section suggestions in config_manager now derive from the `Config` type "
"itself, so they never drift from shipped code (#1508)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:82
msgid ""
"**Plan designs refused at write time (v0.5.1)**: a malformed plan design "
"bounces immediately with the missing sections named, and a refused write "
"restores the scaffold instead of wiping the draft (#1507)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:83
msgid ""
