"release, a run still in flight is waited for, and a commit with no run fails "
"too (#2078)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:113
msgid ""
"**Evolve restarts the right units (v0.5.11)**: the scheduled restart targets "
"resolved unit names instead of the `opencrabs*.service` discovery glob, "
"which also matched the transient unit running the restart and made systemd "
"stop its own executor (#2081)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:114
msgid ""
"**Telegram guests get the full surface (v0.5.12)**: a tag in a chat the bot "
"was never invited to runs the same tool surface, live status block and rich "
"rendering as a normal turn, with one cancellable turn per guest session and "
"rate limiting (#2087, #2109, #2133, #2135, #2138, #2143)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:115
msgid ""
"**A plan is required past a tool-call threshold (v0.5.12)**: once a turn "
"crosses a threshold of tool calls the agent must stop and write a plan "
"before it continues (#2128)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:116
msgid ""
"**The transcript survives a session switch (v0.5.12)**: the fold map is "
"keyed by a stable role and timestamp anchor instead of a UUID minted per "
"render, so switching sessions and coming back no longer folds every turn you "
"had opened (#2155)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:117
msgid ""
"**Headless installs provision the built-in provider (v0.5.12)**: `opencrabs "
"run`, `daemon`, `agent`, `acp` and `cron` mint the built-in token on a fresh "
"home the way the TUI already did, while `status` and `doctor` stay read-only "
"(#2151)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:119
msgid ""
"**doctor --fix repair mode (v0.3.83)**: stuck cron rows, stale markers and "
"broken permissions are repaired on the spot instead of only reported"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:120
msgid ""
"**Per-path write locks (v0.3.83)**: concurrent writes to the same file "
"serialize; the last writer no longer silently wins"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:121
msgid ""
