#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:51
msgid "Provider Priority"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:53
msgid ""
"When multiple providers are enabled, the first one found in this order is "
"used for new sessions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:55
msgid "MiniMax > OpenRouter > Anthropic > OpenAI > Gemini > Custom"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:57
msgid ""
"Each session remembers which provider and model it was using. Switch "
"providers per-session via `/models`."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:59
msgid "Config Safety (v0.3.74)"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:61
msgid ""
"A malformed line in `config.toml` or `keys.toml` corrupts the whole file and "
"takes the agent down (no provider keys, no bot token, no way back in). "
"v0.3.74 makes that class of failure nearly impossible:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:63
msgid ""
"**Config edits via config_manager only**: the agent edits `config.toml` / "
"`keys.toml` only through the `config_manager` tool, never with raw file "
"edits. The write path validates the result and refuses anything that would "
"break parsing (#715)."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:64
msgid ""
"**Guard config-breaking writes**: `edit_file` / `write_file` writes that "
"would break `config.toml` / `keys.toml` are denied outright (#713)."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:65
msgid ""
"**Re-validate before write**: config is re-validated immediately before "
"`fs::write` in the `config_manager` write paths (#714)."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:66
msgid ""
"**Validate keys before snapshot**: `keys.toml` is validated before it is "
"saved as the last-good snapshot, so a bad snapshot can't poison recovery "
"(#712)."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:68
msgid "**v0.3.79 hardened this further:**"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:70
msgid ""
"**Every config write is atomic** (#911): a crash or a concurrent reader "
"mid-write can never observe a half-written `config.toml` or `keys.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:71
msgid ""
"**Config loads no longer race on shared state**, concurrent reloads can't "
"interleave and leave a torn config in memory."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:72
msgid ""
"**Reload failures are specific**: a failed reload says _what_ failed, and a "
"write race is named as the transient condition it is instead of a scary "
"generic error."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:73
msgid ""
"**Never select a provider you didn't configure**, fallback and model routing "
"can no longer land on a provider section that doesn't exist in your config."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:75
msgid "Agent Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:77
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[agent]\n"
"working_directory = \"/path/to/default/dir\"\n"
"thinking = \"on\"                     # \"on\", \"off\", or \"budget_XXk\"\n"
"approval_policy = \"auto-always\"     # \"ask\", \"auto-session\", "
"\"auto-always\"\n"
"max_concurrent = 4                  # max parallel tool calls\n"
"context_limit = 200000              # context window cap (tokens)\n"
"max_tokens = 65536                  # max output tokens per API call\n"
"auto_update = true                  # auto-install releases on startup\n"
"silent_compaction = false           # suppress post-compaction personality "
"narration\n"
"compaction_notice = false            # show the compaction notice pair; off "
"by default (v0.5.4)\n"
"lazy_tools = true                   # JIT tool-schema loading (ships core + "
"tool_search only)\n"
"redact_sensitive_data = true        # redact API keys, tokens, passwords, "
"IPs from output\n"
"debug_logs = false                  # enable debug file logging "
"(hot-reloads, no restart)\n"
"default_provider = \"minimax\"        # fallback provider when no provider "
"is active (v0.3.62)\n"
"default_model = \"MiniMax-M2.7\"      # fallback model when no model is "
"active (v0.3.62)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

