#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:398
msgid "Voice Provider Fallback"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:400
msgid ""
"STT and TTS providers support automatic failover via `fallback_chain`. When "
"the primary returns a 5xx, fails a liveness probe (Voicebox), or is "
"otherwise unreachable, the dispatcher walks the chain in order and tries "
"each entry that has the credentials/config it needs."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:402
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.stt]\n"
"fallback_chain = [\"groq\", \"openai_compatible\", \"local\"]\n"
"\n"
"[providers.tts]\n"
"fallback_chain = [\"openai_compatible\", \"openai\", \"local\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:410
msgid "Chain"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:410
msgid "Valid labels"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:412
msgid "**STT**"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:412
msgid ""
"`voicebox`, `openai_compatible`, `groq`, `local` (aliases: `whisper`, "
"`local_whisper`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:413
msgid "**TTS**"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:413
msgid ""
"`voicebox`, `openai_compatible`, `openai`, `local` (aliases: `piper`, "
"`local_piper`). `groq` is STT-only, the TTS chain rejects it"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:415
msgid ""
"Empty or omitted chain means \"use the default priority order with the "
"primary removed.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:417
msgid "TOML Bash Blocklist (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:419
msgid ""
"A new **TOML-driven bash blocklist** provides runtime-configurable safety "
"gates for shell commands. The blocklist lives in a TOML file and defines "
"patterns that the agent's `bash` tool will refuse to execute:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:421
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# safety.toml (example)\n"
"[bash_blocklist]\n"
"patterns = [\"rm -rf /\", \"dd if=\", \"mkfs\", \":(){ :|:& };:\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:427
msgid "Patterns are matched against the command string before execution"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:428
msgid "The blocklist **reloads on file change** (no restart needed)"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:429
msgid ""
"Configurable per-profile, so different environments can have different "
"safety gates"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:430
msgid "Blocked commands return a clear error explaining which pattern matched"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:432
msgid ""
"This replaces hardcoded safety checks with a user-extensible system. You can "
"add project-specific dangerous commands without code changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:434
msgid "Safety TOML Reload (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/configuration.md:436
msgid ""
"All safety-related TOML files (bash blocklist, brain verification rules) now "
"**hot-reload on change**. Edit the file and the new rules take effect "
"immediately on the next tool call. No restart, no `/reload`, no config "
"manager dance."
msgstr ""

