msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/cli-commands.md:66
msgid ""
"`/doctor`, `/help`, `/usage`, `/evolve`, `/restart`, `/exit`, and system "
"commands work directly on Telegram, Discord, Slack, and WhatsApp without "
"going through the LLM. They execute instantly and return results in the "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/cli-commands.md:68
msgid ""
"`/restart` and `/exit` announce themselves before acting, because once the "
"process is gone nothing is left to report a failure. Both are owner-only, "
"like every other command that changes the running process. `/exit` is the "
"one command with no way back from chat: recovering needs access to the "
"machine OpenCrabs runs on."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/cli-commands.md:70
