#: src/features/document-generation.md:14
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:26
msgid "**One provider active at a time** per session: switch with `/models`"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:27
msgid ""
"**Per-session isolation**: each session remembers its own provider and "
"model. Changing provider in the TUI does not affect other active sessions "
"(Telegram, Discord, Slack)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:28
msgid ""
"**Fallback chain**: configure automatic failover when the primary provider "
"goes down"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:29
msgid ""
"**Models fetched live**: no binary update needed when providers add new "
"models"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:30
msgid ""
"**Function calling detection**: OpenCrabs detects when a model doesn't "
"support tool use and warns you with a model switch suggestion, rather than "
"silently failing"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:31
msgid ""
"**`tool_choice: \"auto\"`**: sent automatically for OpenAI-compatible "
"providers when tools are active, enabling function calling on models that "
"require explicit opt-in"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:32
msgid ""
"**`vision_model` works on ANY provider**: add `vision_model = \"...\"` to "
"any built-in or custom provider block and the agent routes incoming images "
"through that model on the same endpoint. No second API key, no Gemini "
"dependency. See [Image Generation & Vision](./images.md) for the full "
"two-path setup"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:34
msgid "Custom Provider Onboarding (v0.3.24)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:36
msgid "Adding a custom OpenAI-compatible provider is now smoother:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:38
msgid ""
"**Paste-by-default**: `Ctrl+V` / `Cmd+V` on the API key field pastes "
"immediately, no need to tab into the field first"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:39
msgid ""
"**Enter-to-load**: type a model name not in the fetched list and press "
"Enter, it's added to the list and selected"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:40
msgid ""
"**Field refresh**: saved values (base URL, API key, model list) appear "
"instantly without restarting the dialog"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:42
msgid "Provider Registry (v0.3.34)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:44
msgid ""
"All provider resolution now routes through a single registry source of "
"truth: no more hardcoded if-else ladders scattered across the codebase. The "
"registry correctly enforces `api_key` requirements for API providers "
"(Anthropic, OpenAI, GitHub Copilot, Gemini, OpenRouter, MiniMax), so "
"resolution skips them cleanly when keys are missing instead of silently "
"falling back. Adding a new provider is now a one-file change."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:46
msgid "Retry & Fallback Overhaul (v0.3.36)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:48
msgid "The provider retry and fallback system was rebuilt for reliability:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:50
msgid ""
"**Patient backoff**: defaults changed from 100ms hammering to 1s / 2s / 4s / "
"8s, giving rate-limited endpoints time to recover"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:51
msgid ""
"**In-place rate limit retry**: hits 3 retries on the same provider before "
"falling through the fallback chain, preventing unnecessary provider switches"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:52
msgid ""
"**Full fallback chain on any HTTP error**: previously only 5xx/429 triggered "
"fallback; now any HTTP error walks the chain"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:53
msgid ""
"**Fail fast on hard-down endpoints**: DNS failures and connection refused "
"bail immediately instead of wasting retries"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:54
msgid ""
"**Retry events surfaced to user**: each retry shows as `RetryAttempt 1/3 - "
"rate_limit_exceeded` so you always know what's happening"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:55
msgid ""
"**Transient 4xx HTML pages retried**: Cloudflare/nginx error pages that look "
"like 4xx but are actually transient infra issues are now retried"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:57
msgid "Qwen Cache Auto-Enable (v0.3.30)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:59
msgid ""
"Custom providers targeting Qwen-shaped endpoints (base URLs containing "
"`dashscope`, `aliyun`, `aliyuncs`, `dialagram`, or models prefixed with "
"`qwen-*`) automatically get ephemeral `cache_control` markers on the system "
"prompt, last streaming message, and last tool call. Zero-config cost savings "
"for Qwen custom providers, no API key or flag needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:61
msgid "Qwen Tool-Call Leak Strip (v0.3.35)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:63
msgid ""
"Qwen models sometimes emit bare JSON tool-call objects like "
"`{\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}` directly in the "
"content text instead of through the proper tool-call API. A new "
"`bare_tool_call_extractor` detects and strips these leaks so they don't "
"appear as raw JSON in the chat output."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:65
msgid "`/models` Picker (v0.3.30)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:67
msgid ""
"The `/models` command now surfaces **every known provider** including "
"unconfigured ones, marked with a 🔒 lock icon and setup help text. This helps "
"users discover available providers without needing to know which ones need "
"API keys. Custom providers with no configured models show a helpful "
"empty-state message instead of an inert button."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:69
msgid "OpenRouter Reasoning"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:71
msgid ""
"For models that support extended reasoning (e.g. Qwen 3.6 Plus), OpenCrabs "
"sends `include_reasoning: true` automatically when using OpenRouter. "
"Thinking/reasoning output is displayed in collapsible sections:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers-overview.md:78
msgid "Reasoning text wraps to screen width instead of truncating."
msgstr ""

