#: src/brain/providers.md:385
msgid "Fallback Provider Chain"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:387
msgid ""
"Configure automatic failover when the primary provider fails (rate limits, "
"outages, errors). Fallbacks are tried in order until one succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:389
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# config.toml\n"
"[providers.fallback]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"providers = [\"openrouter\", \"anthropic\"]  # Tried in order on failure\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:396
msgid ""
"Each fallback provider must have its API key configured in `keys.toml`. Both "
"`complete()` and `stream()` calls are retried transparently, no changes "
"needed downstream."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:398
msgid "Single fallback shorthand:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:400
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.fallback]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"provider = \"openrouter\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:406
msgid ""
"Or just ask your Crab: _\"Set up fallback providers using openrouter and "
"anthropic\"_, it will configure `config.toml` for you at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:408
msgid "Quota Circuit Breaker (v0.3.79)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:410
msgid ""
"Fallback chains now know the difference between a provider that is "
"momentarily busy and one that is genuinely out of quota."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:412
msgid ""
"**Hard quota exhaustion** (your account has run out of credits/allowance for "
"the period) trips a TTL circuit breaker on that provider. While the breaker "
"is open the provider is **skipped in fallback walks** instead of being "
"retried pointlessly, so failover lands on a provider that can actually serve "
"the request."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:413
msgid ""
"**Transient throttles** (short rate limits, 429s that clear in seconds) are "
"classified separately and retried as before, they never trip the breaker."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:414
msgid ""
"When **every provider in the chain is exhausted**, the failure is reported "
"explicitly as chain exhaustion rather than surfacing as a confusing error "
"from the last provider tried."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:415
msgid ""
"**Retry notices** now name the provider and model being retried, and state "
"whether the cause was a quota exhaustion or a transient throttle."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:417
msgid ""
"No configuration needed: it is always on whenever a fallback chain is "
"configured."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:419
msgid "Fallback Improvements (v0.3.80)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:421
msgid ""
"**Proactive setup suggestion** (#1008): when no fallback chain is "
"configured, OpenCrabs makes a one-shot suggestion to set one up, ask once, "
"answered once, never nags again."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:422
msgid ""
"**HTTP 400 failover guidance** (#1006, #1007): a 400-series failure now "
"carries guidance on what to check, and a chain-exhaustion ledger records why "
"each provider in the chain was ruled out."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:423
msgid ""
