#: src/brain/providers.md:461
msgid "Force Default Provider"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:463
msgid ""
"When you set `force_default = true` on a provider section, a config reload "
"pushes that provider's default pair (provider + model) to **every "
"non-archived session**, overriding their stored pairs. This enforces your "
"chosen default across all active sessions instead of just new ones."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:465
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# config.toml\n"
"[providers.minimax]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"default_model = \"MiniMax-M2.7\"\n"
"force_default = true  # Pushes MiniMax M2.7 to all sessions on reload\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:473
msgid "**How it works:**"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:474
msgid ""
"Only fires when the flagged section is the **active default provider** (set "
"via `/models` or `default_provider` in `[agent]`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:475
msgid "Archived sessions are never touched"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:476
msgid "Sessions already on the target pair are skipped"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:477
msgid ""
"Without this flag: defaults apply to new sessions only, existing sessions "
"keep their own provider/model"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:479
msgid ""
"**Use case:** You want to roll out a new default model (e.g. MiniMax M2.7) "
"across all active sessions immediately, not just new ones. Set "
"`force_default = true` on the MiniMax section, reload config, and every "
"session switches to M2.7."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:481
msgid ""
"**Note:** This only reinforces the default, it doesn't override a different "
"active provider. If a session is using Anthropic Claude and you set "
"`force_default = true` on MiniMax, the Claude session stays on Claude "
"(because MiniMax isn't the active default)."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:483
msgid "Vision Model"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:485
msgid ""
"When your default chat model doesn't support vision, set `vision_model` to a "
"vision-capable model on the same provider. This registers a vision tool that "
"the agent can call, it sends the image to the vision model, gets a "
"description back, and the chat model uses that context to reply."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:487
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# config.toml\n"
"[providers.minimax]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"default_model = \"MiniMax-M2.5\"\n"
"vision_model = \"MiniMax-Text-01\"  # Agent calls vision tool → this model "
"describes image → M2.5 replies\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:495
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.openai]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"default_model = \"gpt-5-nano\"\n"
"vision_model = \"gpt-5-nano\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:502
msgid ""
"MiniMax auto-configures `vision_model = \"MiniMax-Text-01\"` on first run. "
"You can also ask your Crab to set it up: _\"Configure vision model for "
"MiniMax\"_, it will update `config.toml` at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:504
msgid ""
"This is separate from the [Gemini image tools](./images.md) which provide "
"dedicated `generate_image` and `analyze_image` tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:506
msgid "Per-Session Providers"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:508
msgid ""
"Each session remembers its provider and model. Switch to Claude in one "
"session, Gemini in another, switching sessions restores the provider "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:510
msgid "Model Picker (v0.3.75)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:512
msgid "The `/models` picker got a real overhaul:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:514
msgid ""
"**Opus 5 surfaced**: Opus 5 now shows up via a third parallel list plus "
"state discovery."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:515
msgid ""
"**Newest-first ordering**: models are ordered newest-first instead of by "
"merge order."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:516
msgid ""
"**claude-cli model discovery**: the claude-cli model list is discovered live "
"from the CLI instead of being hardcoded, with every claude-cli row formatted "
"consistently."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:517
msgid ""
"**Reconciled against live inventory**: the picker reconciles against the "
"live model inventory so it never offers a model that isn't actually "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:519
msgid "Natural Model Naming (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:521
msgid ""
"The `/models` command now accepts **colloquial model names**. Instead of "
"typing the exact model ID, you can say it the way people talk:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:530
msgid ""
"The resolver normalizes spacing, case, and common abbreviations before "
"matching against the provider's model list. Exact matches still take "
"priority."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:532
msgid "Plan/Execute Provider Routing (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:534
msgid ""
"The `/plan` and `/execute` commands can now route onto **their own dedicated "
"provider and model**, separate from the main chat provider:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:536
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# config.toml\n"
"[agent]\n"
"plan_provider = \"anthropic\"\n"
"plan_model = \"claude-opus-4-8\"\n"
"execute_provider = \"openrouter\"\n"
"execute_model = \"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/providers.md:545
msgid ""
"This lets you use a stronger model for planning (where reasoning quality "
"matters most) and a faster/cheaper model for execution (where throughput "
"matters). If unset, both fall back to the session's active provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:3
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs supports **image generation** (text-to-image and img2img) and "
"**vision analysis** (image-to-text). Vision works through two paths, pick "
"whichever fits your provider setup."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:5
msgid "Vision: Two Paths"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:7
msgid "Path A: `vision_model` on Your Active Provider (Preferred)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:9
msgid ""
"Set `vision_model = \"<model>\"` inside the provider block you're already "
"using. Works for **every** built-in and custom provider. No second API key "
"needed, the agent calls `analyze_image` against the vision model on the "
"**same provider endpoint**."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:11
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# keys.toml\n"
"[providers.openrouter]\n"
"api_key = \"sk-or-...\"\n"
"\n"
"# config.toml\n"
"[providers.openrouter]\n"
"model = \"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4\"\n"
"vision_model = \"google/gemini-2.5-flash\"   # ← any vision-capable model on "
"the same endpoint\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:22
msgid ""
"When a user sends an image and the chat model can't handle it natively, the "
"agent routes the image through `vision_model`, gets a text description back, "
"and replies with that context."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:24
msgid ""
"**Example:** User sends an image while you're on MiniMax M2.5 (no native "
"vision). The agent calls the vision tool, which sends the image to "
"`MiniMax-Text-01` (or any model you set), gets the description, and M2.5 "
"replies using that context."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:26
msgid "**Why this is preferred:**"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:27
msgid "Single API key, single billing account"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:28
msgid ""
"Works on any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (OpenRouter, Ollama, LM Studio, "
"vLLM, Groq, custom)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:29
msgid ""
"No extra onboarding step: just add one line to your existing provider block"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:31
msgid "Path B: Gemini Global Fallback"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:33
msgid ""
"Use this only when your active provider has **no** vision-capable model. "
"Gemini acts as a dedicated vision+image backend, independent of your chat "
"provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:35
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# keys.toml\n"
"[image]\n"
"api_key = \"AIza...\"    # ← MUST go here. See gotcha below.\n"
"\n"
"# config.toml\n"
"[image.generation]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"model = \"gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\"\n"
"\n"
"[image.vision]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"model = \"gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:50
msgid ""
"Get a free API key from [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com). "
"Configure interactively with `/onboard:image`."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:52
msgid "⚠️ Gotcha: `#[serde(skip)]` on `[image.vision] api_key`"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:54
msgid ""
"The `api_key` field under `[image.vision]` in `config.toml` is silently "
"ignored: it's marked `#[serde(skip)]` in the source. **Always put the Gemini "
"key in `keys.toml` under `[image]`**, never in `config.toml`. If vision "
"reports as unavailable despite a key being set, this is almost always the "
"cause."
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:56
msgid "Diagnostic: Why Is Vision Unavailable?"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:58
msgid ""
"`is_vision_available` logs the exact reason at INFO level with "
"`target=vision`. Search your daily log:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:61
msgid "'target=vision'"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:64
msgid "Common causes surfaced:"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:65
msgid ""
"Missing `vision_model` on active provider (the only field actually required "
"since v0.3.64)"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:66
msgid "Missing `api_key` for that provider"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:67
msgid "Missing Gemini `[image] api_key` in `keys.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:68
msgid "Key placed in `config.toml` where `#[serde(skip)]` drops it"
msgstr ""

#: src/brain/images.md:70
msgid ""
"**v0.3.64 change:** setting `vision_model` on your active provider is now "
"sufficient to enable vision. The `enabled` flag under `[image.vision]` is no "
"longer required. The vision roll-through tries each provider endpoint and "
"falls back to Gemini last."
msgstr ""

