#: src/channels/overview.md:59
msgid "Cross-Channel Session Resolution (v0.3.29)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:61
msgid ""
"All messaging channels now share a stable `[chat:<id>]` suffix pattern for "
"reliable session lookup. Previously only Telegram had this; Discord, Slack, "
"and WhatsApp used exact-title matching which broke when the agent "
"auto-renamed sessions (creating duplicates on every message)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:63
msgid "The shared `channels::session_resolve` module provides:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:64
msgid ""
"**Suffix-first lookup**: fast path using `[chat:discord-dm-<user_id>]`, "
"`[chat:slack-<channel_id>]`, `[chat:wa-<phone>]` etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:65
msgid ""
"**Legacy forward-migration**: pre-suffix rows are migrated to the suffix "
"format on first lookup"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:66
msgid ""
"**`/sessions` binding**: explicit chat→session binding on switch so user "
"choices win over suffix lookup"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:68
msgid "Follow-Up Cancel (v0.3.30)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:70
msgid ""
"Sending a message while the agent is mid-run now acts as **ESC x2** (cancel "
"current run) across all channels. The cancelled partial content is "
"preserved, and the new message starts a fresh agent turn."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:72
msgid "ZIP Attachments (v0.3.30)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:74
msgid "ZIP file attachments from users are extracted and processed inline:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:75
msgid "Text files are inlined into the conversation"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:76
msgid "Images get vision markers for multimodal processing"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:77
msgid "PDFs get text extraction"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:78
msgid "Capped at **50 files / 10 MB** per ZIP entry"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:80
msgid "Group Onboarding & /cowork (v0.3.74)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:82
msgid "Getting a bot into a group and making it useful is now a single flow:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:84
msgid ""
"**/cowork opens the group**: `/cowork` sets the target group `open = true` "
"and persists it (#718)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:85
msgid ""
"**/cowork admin deep link**: the `/cowork` deep link requests admin rights, "
"so the bot joins already promoted (#709)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:86
msgid ""
"**Group onboarding greeting**: the bot greets the group with an onboarding "
"nudge when it joins (#707, #708)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:87
msgid ""
"**Per-group /start registration**: `/start` in a group registers the member "
"per-group instead of the stale `config.toml` lecture (#708)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:88
msgid ""
"**Register joining members**: any member who joins a bot group is "
"auto-registered (#710)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:89
msgid ""
"**Secure by default**: member auto-registration is gated to `open = true` "
"groups (#717)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:91
msgid "Follow-Up Suggestions (v0.3.74)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:93
msgid ""
"**follow_up_question degrades gracefully**: returns the question as plain "
"text on non-interactive surfaces (#716)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:94
msgid ""
"**Telegram follow-up taps**: `suggest_followups` renders last, fixing taps "
"doing nothing (#723, #724)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:95
msgid ""
"**Accurate description**: the `suggest_followups` tool description is "
"channel-accurate, so the model invokes it instead of writing plain-text "
"suggestions (#706)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/overview.md:96
msgid ""
"**Outbound media dedup**: an identical file+caption re-uploaded to the same "
"chat within a short window is collapsed, so the agent can't send it twice "
"(#721)."
msgstr ""

