#: src/channels/telegram.md:47
msgid "**DMs and groups**: Works in private chats and group conversations"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:48
msgid ""
"**Forum topic routing** (v0.3.31): In supergroups with topics enabled, the "
"bot tracks `thread_id` through the full pipeline. Use `list_topics` action "
"to map topic names (e.g. `#announcements`) to numeric IDs, then pass "
"`thread_id` to `send` / `reply` / `send_photo` to route into a specific topic"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:49
msgid ""
"**Context-aware pre-tool status** (v0.3.31): While a tool runs, the bot "
"shows a live status message naming the tool, elapsed time, and either a "
"reasoning excerpt or an anchored phrase from the user's request"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:50
msgid ""
"**Inline ctx budget footer** (v0.3.36): context budget footer (`ctx: XK/YK "
"Z% | N tok/s`) is now appended to the last response message instead of sent "
"as a separate message. Keeps the chat clean."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:52
msgid "v0.3.76–v0.3.78 Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:54
msgid "/new Gating (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:55
msgid ""
"The `/new` command is now **gated to the bot owner** in group chats. "
"Non-owners cannot create new sessions or reset context. The command menu is "
"also scoped: owners see the full menu, non-owners see only the commands "
"available to them."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:57
msgid "HTML Conversion (v0.3.77)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:58
msgid ""
"All `telegram_send` actions now apply **HTML-to-Telegram conversion** "
"consistently. Previously, only the main response path converted HTML "
"entities; proactive sends, follow-ups, and media captions could arrive with "
"raw `<b>` tags or unescaped ampersands."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:60
msgid "Rich Delivery (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:61
msgid ""
"Telegram delivery is unified on **markdown formatting**. The legacy \"blocks "
"path\" (which sent structured JSON blocks) has been removed in favor of a "
"single rich-markdown renderer. This eliminates formatting inconsistencies "
"between streaming responses and proactive sends."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:63
msgid "Callback Routing (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:64
msgid ""
"Inline keyboard callbacks (plan approvals, follow-up taps, dedup approvals) "
"now route to the **originating session** instead of the chat-bound session. "
"Previously, tapping a button in a group chat could route the callback to the "
"wrong session if multiple sessions shared the same chat."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:66
msgid "Background Streaming (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:67
msgid ""
"Background task results now stream through **one turn per session** instead "
"of spawning a new message per tick. This eliminates the message flood when a "
"background task (build, test suite) produces incremental output."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:69
msgid "Follow-Up Attribution (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:70
msgid ""
"When a user taps a follow-up suggestion button in a group chat, the agent "
"now **names the member** who tapped it. Previously, follow-up taps were "
"anonymous in group contexts."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:72
msgid "Other Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:73
msgid "`/start` recognizes existing members of closed groups (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:74
msgid ""
"Plan-card serialisation prevents duplicate cards on concurrent refreshes "
"(v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:75
msgid "Follow-up taps run a real tools turn instead of echoing text (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:76
msgid "Flow block no longer posts a new message every tick (v0.3.77)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:77
msgid "Echoed plan titles dropped from responses (v0.3.77)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:78
msgid "Open-group registration gated on persisted open flag (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:79
msgid "Cowork members recorded on first message (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:80
msgid ""
"**Rolling status edit-in-place** (v0.3.36): tool status messages (⚙️ "
"running, ✅ done) are edited in-place instead of delete+recreate, preventing "
"flicker and preserving scroll position."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:81
msgid ""
"**Bot command hot-reload** (v0.3.36): bot commands refresh automatically "
"when config or skills change, without restarting the bot."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:82
msgid ""
"**Guard tok/s against burst-delivery** (v0.3.36): tok/s footer is guarded "
"against burst-delivery artifacts so the number stays stable."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:83
msgid ""
"**`follow_up_question` polish** (v0.3.34): Telegram keyboard is now "
"single-column with a 40-character label cap (longer options rejected with a "
"clear error). The rolling \"Running follow_up_question (16s)\" status is "
"suppressed while the keyboard is pending so buttons don't get visually "
"buried. The LLM is instructed to call the tool silently without echoing the "
"question text in surrounding prose"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:84
msgid ""
"**Inline buttons**: Provider picker, model picker, session switcher use "
"Telegram inline keyboards"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:85
msgid "**Image support**: Send images to the bot, receive generated images"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:86 src/channels/whatsapp.md:74
#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:117
msgid "**Voice messages**: STT transcription + TTS response"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:87
msgid ""
"**All slash commands**: `/help`, `/models`, `/new`, `/sessions`, custom "
"commands"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:88
msgid ""
"**Owner vs non-owner**: Owner uses the shared TUI session, non-owners get "
"per-user sessions"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:89
msgid ""
"**Onboarding overhaul** (v0.3.30): Auto-detects owner user ID from "
"`getUpdates`, persists partial config on cancel, only Enter on the last step "
"commits (Tab no longer silently rewrites ~30 config keys)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:90
msgid ""
"**Teloxide upgrade + join detection** (v0.3.35): Upgraded from teloxide 0.13 "
"to 0.17. New members joining a group are now detected before the allowlist "
"check, so the bot can greet or moderate join events. Marathon-bucket rolling "
"status rotates through project-author quip pool for more varied status "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:92
msgid "v0.3.81 Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:94
msgid "Mermaid Diagrams as Images (#1044)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:95
msgid ""
"Mermaid code fences in rich messages render as **images** via the "
"markdown+media route, while **tables stay native** Telegram formatting "
"instead of being rasterized into the image."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:97
msgid "Delivery and Rate-Limit Hardening"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:98
msgid ""
"**Rich blocks decode as a typed AST** (#1058) instead of ad-hoc string "
"surgery, so structured messages can't arrive mangled"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:99
msgid ""
"**Inline rate-limit waits capped at 30s** (#1064): a Telegram 429 never "
"parks a turn indefinitely"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:100
msgid ""
"**Flow footer + section cap** (#1052, #1053, #1054, #1056): flow logs get a "
"footer and bounded sections instead of unbounded message growth"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:102
msgid "Group Safety"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:103
msgid "**Only the owner may add the bot to a group** (#1042)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:104
msgid ""
"**Bot-add detection** (#1041): being added by a member is told apart from "
"another bot arriving"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:105
msgid ""
"**Unauthorised chats are never recorded** (#1043): chats that were never "
"approved leave no session residue"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:107
msgid "v0.3.82 Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:109
msgid "Long Rate-Limit Windows Bail Immediately (#1110)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:110
msgid ""
"A Telegram 429 that asks for a long wait no longer sleeps inline. The send "
"returns immediately and the work is rescheduled, instead of the turn parking "
"on a multi-minute (or multi-hour) window. This closes the failure mode where "
"one throttled send held a turn open long enough to look like a hang."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:112
msgid "Delivery Correctness"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:113
msgid ""
"**Rich sends stop building a double-slash URL** (#1117): a trailing slash on "
"the API base no longer produces `//bot<token>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:114
msgid ""
"**Rich API calls honour `set_api_url`** (#1088): the rich path used a "
"hardcoded `api.telegram.org`, so it bypassed a redirected Bot. It now routes "
"through the caller's API URL like every other method, which also makes the "
"path testable without a real network call"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:115
msgid ""
"**All six send arms route through thread resolution**: forum-topic targeting "
"is applied consistently instead of on some arms only"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:117
msgid "Observability"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:118
msgid ""
"**Send-correlation telemetry** (#1085): the three send chokepoints, every "
"`telegram_send` arm, and the final streaming edit-in-place are all logged, "
"so a message that never arrived can be traced to the arm that dropped it"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:122
msgid ""
"All Telegram options live under `[channels.telegram]` in "
"`~/.opencrabs/config.toml`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:124
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[channels.telegram]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"token = \"123456:ABC-DEF...\"          # or store in keys.toml\n"
"allowed_users = [\"123456789\"]         # numeric Telegram user IDs\n"
"allowed_channels = [\"-100123456\"]     # restrict to specific group/channel "
"IDs (empty = all)\n"
"respond_to = \"mention\"                # \"all\", \"dm_only\", \"mention\" "
"(default)\n"
"session_idle_hours = 24.0             # idle timeout for non-owner sessions\n"
"rich_messages = false                 # native Telegram rich messages (Bot "
"API 10.1)\n"
"silence_group_start = true            # silently ignore /start from "
"non-allowed users in groups\n"
"bot_owner = [\"123456789\"]             # owner IDs (gated commands, /cd "
"hidden dirs, /profiles)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:145
msgid "`true` (since v0.3.64)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:145
msgid ""
"Send structured replies as native Telegram rich messages (tables, headings, "
"lists, math). Requires current mobile/desktop Telegram clients. Telegram Web "
"and older clients show a \"not supported\" placeholder. Toggle via the "
"onboarding checkbox or config"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:147
msgid ""
"Bot owner user IDs. Owners can access gated commands (/profiles, hidden "
"files in /cd), manage profiles. Defaults to first entry in `allowed_users`"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:148
msgid "`guest_queries`"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:148
msgid ""
"Answer Telegram Guest Mode tags: someone tags the bot in a chat it is not a "
"member of and gets one reply there. Callers must be the owner, an admin, or "
"listed for that chat. See [Guest queries](#guest-queries)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:150
msgid "Per-group access control (per-chat ACL)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:152
msgid ""
"Telegram groups can have their own member list, so a user can be allowed in "
"one group without gaining DM access:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:154
msgid ""
"`allowed_users` (channel level): **admins**: may DM the bot and act in any "
"chat."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:155
msgid "`bot_owner`: the **owner**: always allowed everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:156
msgid ""
"`[channels.telegram.groups.<chat_id>].allowed_users`: allowed in that group "
"only. These users are refused in DMs unless they are also an admin or the "
"owner, which closes the \"DM the bot privately to escape group oversight\" "
"bypass."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:158
msgid ""
"DMs are gated to admins + owner. If neither `allowed_users` nor `bot_owner` "
"is set, the bot is unconfigured and stays open (no hard lockout); set either "
"one to lock it down."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:160
msgid "Each group can also override `respond_to` just for itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:162
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[channels.telegram]\n"
"allowed_users = [\"111\"]                  # admins: DM + any chat\n"
"respond_to = \"mention\"                   # global default\n"
"\n"
"[channels.telegram.groups.-1001234567890]\n"
"allowed_users = [\"222\", \"333\"]           # allowed in this group only, "
"never via DM\n"
"respond_to = \"all\"                       # per-group override of the "
"global respond_to\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:172
msgid ""
"`respond_to` accepts `all`, `mention`, `dm_only`, or `auto` (reply to all "
"while there is at most one active sender, then switch to mention-only once a "
"second unique sender appears)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:174
msgid "Per-group open mode (v0.3.66)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:176
msgid ""
"Set `open = true` on a trusted group to serve all members without individual "
"allowlisting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:183
msgid ""
"Use this for public/community groups where you want the bot available to "
"everyone. Members still can't DM the bot unless they're in the global "
"`allowed_users` or `bot_owner`."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:185
msgid "Guest queries"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:187
msgid ""
"Telegram Guest Mode (Bot API 10.0) lets someone tag `@yourbot` in a chat the "
"bot is **not** a member of. With `guest_queries = true`, OpenCrabs answers "
"the tag right there using the API method `answerGuestQuery`."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:189
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[channels.telegram]\n"
"guest_queries = true                     # default false: guest tags are "
"ignored\n"
"allowed_users = [\"111\"]                  # admins: answered anywhere\n"
"[channels.telegram.groups.-1001234567890]\n"
"allowed_users = [\"222\"]                  # this user is answered in this "
"chat only\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:197
msgid ""
"Default is off, and the gate is narrow once it is on. The caller must be the "
"`bot_owner`, an admin (`allowed_users`), or listed for **that** chat. A "
"group's `open = true` grants nothing here: it opens that group to the bot, "
"it does not authorize answering guest tags from its members. Refused queries "
"are logged with the `guest_query_id`, the caller, and the chat."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:199
msgid "Boundaries of a guest turn:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:201
msgid ""
"The bot sees only the tagged message, no history from that chat, and nothing "
"from the guest turn is stored in that chat's history."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:202
msgid ""
"A guest turn runs the same tool surface as a normal turn, with one "
"exception: tools that need approval are denied, because approvals are "
"buttons in a chat and the caller is not the machine's owner. The tool set is "
"capped at what a stranger should reach (#2134)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:203
msgid ""
"The live status block and rich rendering match a normal turn: the guest sees "
"the same progress chrome and the same markdown or rich reply, and an edit "
"replaces the placeholder rather than appending a second message (#2109, "
"#2133, #2135, #2138)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:204
msgid ""
"One guest turn per session at a time, cancellable, behind a rate limit, so a "
"tag storm cannot fan out into parallel turns (#2143)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:205
msgid ""
"A reply with no tool calls is the answer alone, and the answer is never "
"carried twice in one reply (#2113)."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:206
msgid ""
"Channel directives (`<<...>>`) are stripped, so a local file path can never "
"leak into someone else's chat."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:207
msgid "An overlong reply is cut and marked `[truncated]` rather than dropped."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:209
msgid ""
"Because the pinned `teloxide-core` has no guest update variant, guest "
"queries are read on the raw `getUpdates` layer, and `guest_message` is in "
"the bot's `allowed_updates` list. Nothing to configure for that; it is on "
"whenever the channel runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:211
msgid "Voice and file pickup in groups"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:213
msgid ""
"In mention-only groups (`respond_to = \"mention\"`), users can share files "
"and voice messages even when the bot isn't directly tagged in the same "
"message:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:215
msgid ""
"**Fire-and-forget file capture**: The bot downloads ALL incoming voice, "
"video, document, and audio files from group messages to `~/.opencrabs/tmp/`, "
"regardless of whether the bot was mentioned. This happens silently in the "
"background."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:216
msgid ""
"**Tag-then-ask**: A user sends a voice message, then tags the bot in a "
"follow-up message (e.g. `@bot what did I just say?`). The bot scans the tmp "
"directory for recent voice files from that chat (5-minute window), "
"transcribes the most recent one, and prepends the transcript to the user's "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:218
msgid ""
"This solves the core UX problem in mention-only groups: previously, tagging "
"the bot in the same message as a voice note didn't work because Telegram "
"sends voice and text as separate messages."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:220
msgid ""
"The agent can use `telegram_send` with 20+ actions. The `thread_id` field on "
"`send` / `reply` / `send_photo` targets a specific forum topic in "
"supergroups with topics enabled."
msgstr ""

