#: src/channels/telegram.md:234
msgid "Reactions (v0.3.58)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:236
msgid "The bot understands Telegram emoji reactions in both directions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:238
msgid ""
"**Inbound**: when a user reacts to one of the bot's messages with an emoji, "
"the bot picks up that reaction (it looks up the original bot message by its "
"platform message ID) and can act on it as feedback."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:239
msgid ""
"**Frame reactions (v0.3.61)**: inbound reactions are read by sentiment and "
"the bot addresses the user by first name in its response."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:240
msgid ""
"**Mid-turn reactions (v0.3.61)**: if a user reacts during a running turn, "
"the reaction injects into the current loop instead of spawning a second turn."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:241
msgid ""
"**Reaction-only replies**: when a short acknowledgement says it all (a "
"thumbs-up, a 👀, a 😂), the bot can respond with just a reaction instead of a "
"full text message, keeping the chat uncluttered."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:242
msgid ""
"**Emoji validation**: only real emoji count as reaction directives; code "
"spans and stray characters are ignored, and react directives are stripped "
"from intermediate status messages so they never leak into the visible reply."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:244
msgid ""
"Use the `set_reaction` action on `telegram_send` to add a reaction to a "
"specific message from the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:246
msgid "/cowork: Workspace Creation (v0.3.59)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:248
msgid ""
"`/cowork` creates a team workspace directly from Telegram. Run it in your DM "
"with the bot:"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:250
msgid "Send `/cowork` in your DM with the bot"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:251
msgid "The bot replies with an invite link and QR code for a new group"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:252
msgid "Scan the QR code or tap the link to create the group"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:253
msgid "Add your friends or teammates to the group"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:254
msgid ""
"Members auto-register to the **group's allow list** "
"(`[channels.telegram.groups.<chat_id>].allowed_users`), not the global one. "
"Both new joiners (via invite link) and existing members (on their first "
"message) get registered. Cowork members can talk in the group but cannot DM "
"the bot privately unless also on the global `allowed_users`. The owner gets "
"a confirmation for each registration."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:256
msgid ""
"`/cowork` works from any surface. In Telegram DMs, the native flow activates "
"directly. From the TUI, Discord, Slack, or WhatsApp, the agent calls the "
"`cowork_connect` tool which mints a session, registers it with the bot, and "
"returns the `t.me` deep link plus a scannable QR code PNG."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:258
msgid "Flow Logs (v0.3.63)"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/telegram.md:260
msgid ""
"Telegram's rich API supports 32K-character processing-log blocks. When the "
"agent runs multi-step operations (tool calls, research, code generation), it "
"streams progress into a single flow-log message that grows as the turn "
"progresses. For shorter messages, HTML formatting falls back to plain text."
msgstr ""

