#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:54
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:56
msgid ""
"**One account per instance.** Each OpenCrabs instance supports one WhatsApp "
"account (one companion device). You run the bot AS whatever account you "
"scan: your own number (talk via \"Message Yourself\"), or any other number "
"you own, including a WhatsApp Business account."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:58
msgid ""
"**The bot talks to itself.** If you message the bot's own paired number, the "
"bot replies to you. This is by design. The paired account's self-chat is "
"always allowed, regardless of `response_policy` or `allowed_phones`."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:60
msgid ""
"**Allowlist behavior.** Anyone messaging the paired number who is on the "
"`allowed_phones` list gets a reply. The `response_policy` controls who else "
"can interact beyond the allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:63
msgid ""
"**Ownership (v0.5.1, deny-by-default).** Before v0.5.1 an empty "
"`allowed_phones` under `response_policy = \"auto\"` answered every contact "
"_and_ elevated them all to owner: one forgotten allowlist away from handing "
"strangers `/evolve` and `/cd`. That elevation is gone: being answered no "
"longer means being in charge. Owner status comes from the paired account's "
"self-chat, a configured `bot_owner`, or ownership resolution over "
"`allowed_phones` + `bot_owner`: never from an empty list. Tool-approval "
"replies (Yes/Always/No/YOLO) resolve only for the owner on all four channels."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:72 src/channels/whatsapp.md:115
msgid "**Personal and group chats**: Works in DMs and group conversations"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:75 src/channels/whatsapp.md:118
msgid ""
"**Plain text UI**: No buttons (WhatsApp limitation), uses text-based menus"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:78
msgid "Outbound rate limiting"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:80
msgid ""
"WhatsApp is the channel with the heaviest ban consequences, so every "
"outbound send goes through a budget (since v0.5.1):"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:89
msgid "Mechanism"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:91
msgid "**Per-minute pacing**"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:91
msgid ""
"A token bucket sized to `messages_per_minute` (default 30) refills "
"continuously. An over-budget send is **paced**, not dropped: the caller "
"sleeps for the refill gap and then sends. Set `0` to disable pacing."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:92
msgid "**Rolling daily cap**"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:92
msgid ""
"The 24h window allows `daily_cap` sends (default 800). On saturation further "
"sends park in a FIFO queue; a background drainer flushes them as the window "
"slides. A queued quote-reply loses its quote context, the text still "
"arrives. Set `0` to disable the cap."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:93
msgid "**Owner alert**"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:93
msgid ""
"The first send queued in a saturation episode alerts the bot owner exactly "
"once (through the WhatsApp session), and the alert re-arms when traffic "
"drops back under the cap."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:94
msgid "**Owner bypass**"
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:94
msgid ""
"Messages addressed to the owner skip budget consumption entirely, so you "
"always get fast replies; the saturation alert itself is also exempt."
msgstr ""

#: src/channels/whatsapp.md:96
msgid ""
"Streaming answers used to post every chunk as its own message, exactly the "
"volume pattern Meta's heuristics hunt. Outbound replies now edit one message "
"in place (since v0.5.1), which keeps chunked turns well inside the budget; "
"the limiter is the safety net underneath."
msgstr ""

