#: src/features/sessions.md:134
msgid "Background Tasks (v0.3.74)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:136
msgid ""
"Long-running shell commands no longer block your session. When the agent "
"runs a known-long command (`cargo test`, `cargo build`, `npx remotion "
"render`, `gh run watch`, and similar), OpenCrabs **auto-promotes it to a "
"background task** (#722): the command runs detached, the session is freed "
"immediately, and the agent can keep working (or you can switch away) while "
"it finishes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:138
msgid ""
"When the task completes, the result is injected back into the originating "
"session and **resumes it automatically**. On the TUI the session picks up at "
"the next tool-call boundary; on Telegram the resume is delivered to the same "
"chat (#722). No polling loops, no re-running the command to \"check\", the "
"completion report arrives on its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:140
msgid ""
"The agent is told via its preamble that long tasks run in the background and "
"resume the session when done, so it wraps up or moves on instead of sitting "
"in a wait loop (#722)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:142
msgid "**Two related session fixes landed in the same release:**"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:144
msgid ""
"**No perpetual resume**: a completed session no longer resumes on every "
"restart. Resume turns are not re-tracked as pending requests, so a finished "
"background task stays finished across restarts (#729)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:145
msgid ""
"**No lingering cancelled query**: a query cancelled before the agent "
"replied, plus its empty assistant placeholder, are dropped as a pair so they "
"don't linger in context and duplicate on resend (#730)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:147
msgid "Background-Task Resume Everywhere (v0.3.75)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:149
msgid ""
"v0.3.74 introduced background-task resume on the TUI and Telegram. v0.3.75 "
"extends it to **every channel**: Discord, Slack, WhatsApp, and the "
"interactive CLI agent now resume your session the moment a long task "
"finishes, powered by a shared `bg_resume` helper so the behaviour is "
"identical across surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:151
msgid "A few refinements make background tasks easier to live with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:153
msgid ""
"**Indicator on the input border**: the background-task indicator moved onto "
"the input border, and a detached command shows what it's currently doing."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:154
msgid ""
"**No scaffolding in chat**: a background task's system scaffolding no longer "
"reaches the chat."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:155
msgid ""
"**Restart-killed tasks reported**: background tasks a restart killed are "
"reported instead of leaving the session waiting forever."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:159
msgid ""
"Run multiple sessions side by side with tmux-style pane splitting. Each pane "
"is a fully isolated agent, see [Split Panes](./split-panes.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:161 src/features/split-panes.md:50
msgid "State Management"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:163
msgid "v0.2.92 improved session state tracking:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:165
msgid ""
"**Session reload after cancellation**: After Esc+Esc cancel, session context "
"reloads from DB to pick up any changes made during the cancelled operation"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:166
msgid ""
"**Cached state cleanup**: Deleting a session now clears stale pane cache "
"entries, preventing phantom state on restart"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:167
msgid ""
"**CLI tool segment persistence**: Tool results from CLI providers (Claude "
"CLI, OpenCode CLI) are now saved to DB alongside regular messages, "
"preserving correct text/tool interleaving across restarts"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:168
msgid ""
"**Case-insensitive tool input**: Tool input descriptions use "
"case-insensitive key lookup, fixing failures when providers return different "
"casing"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:170
msgid "Channel Sessions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:172
msgid ""
"All channels (Telegram, Discord, Slack, WhatsApp, Trello) persist sessions "
"in SQLite by channel/group title. Sessions survive process restarts, no more "
"lost context after daemon restart. Each channel group gets its own isolated "
"session, while owner DMs share the TUI session. Cross-channel stable session "
"suffixes (`[chat:<id>]`) ensure reliable session resolution across Discord, "
"Slack, and WhatsApp (v0.3.29)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:174
msgid "Session-Routed Recovery Reports (v0.3.81)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/sessions.md:176
msgid ""
"Crash-recovery reports **route by session** (#1037): a resumed turn reports "
"back to the session that owned it, not to whichever session happened to boot "
"the recovery. Multi-session setups no longer cross-deliver recovery noise."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:3
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs supports tmux-style pane splitting in the TUI. Run multiple "
"sessions side by side, each with its own provider, model, and context, all "
"processing in parallel."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:5
msgid "Splitting"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:9
msgid "Split horizontal"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:9
msgid "`\\|` (pipe)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:10
msgid "Split vertical"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:10
msgid "`_` (underscore)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:11
msgid "Cycle focus"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:12
msgid "Close pane"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:16
msgid ""
"Each pane runs an independent session. You can have one pane writing code "
"with Claude while another reviews tests with Gemini. The status bar shows "
"`[n/total]` to indicate which pane is focused."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:18
msgid ""
"**Independent providers**: Each pane can use a different AI provider and "
"model"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:19
msgid "**Independent context**: Conversation history is isolated per pane"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:20
msgid "**Parallel processing**: All panes process concurrently via Tokio"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:21
msgid ""
"**Persistent sessions**: Each pane's session is saved to SQLite like any "
"other session"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:23
msgid "Example Layout"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:35
msgid "Split vertically with `_`, then horizontally with `|` in the top pane."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:37
msgid "Persistent Layout"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:39
msgid ""
"Split pane configuration (splits, sizes, focused pane) saves to "
"`~/.opencrabs/pane_layout.json` on quit and Ctrl+C. On restart, your layout "
"is restored exactly as you left it. Each restored pane preloads its session "
"messages from the database, so content is visible immediately instead of "
"blank."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:41
msgid "Non-Focused Panes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:43
msgid ""
"Non-focused panes show compact tool call summaries and stripped reasoning "
"text. Tool groups display as single collapsed lines matching the focused "
"pane style. All panes auto-scroll to the bottom when new messages arrive."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:45
msgid "v0.2.92 fixed several rendering issues:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:46
msgid ""
"Tool calls no longer show a perpetual \"running\" spinner after completion"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:47
msgid "Scroll position correctly tracks for inactive panes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:48
msgid "Stale cache is cleared when sessions are updated or deleted"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:52
msgid ""
"Deleting a session now properly cleans up cached pane state. Previously, "
"deleting a session left stale entries in the pane cache, which could cause "
"phantom panes on restart."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:54
msgid "Live Background Updates (v0.3.36)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:56
msgid ""
"Inactive panes now update **live** in the background. Previously, "
"non-focused panes only refreshed when you switched focus to them. Now a "
"background-session live-state cache routes `IntermediateText` and "
"`QueuedUserMessage` events into per-session deltas, so you can watch tool "
"calls and responses appearing in other panes in real time without switching "
"focus."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:58
msgid ""
"**Provider/model contamination prevention:** When closing or switching "
"panes, the old session's provider is captured _before_ the switch. This "
"blocks cross-provider model leaks at 27 call sites throughout the codebase. "
"The footer always shows the correct provider+model for the focused pane."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:60
msgid ""
"**Ctrl+N** binds the focused pane and live-refreshes the footer title, so "
"new sessions show up immediately in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:62
msgid "Reasoning Expand (v0.3.74)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:64
msgid ""
"Reasoning blocks now cycle through **three states** instead of toggling "
"open/closed. Click a reasoning block (or press `Ctrl+O`) to cycle: "
"**collapsed → capped → full**. The capped middle state shows a bounded "
"preview so a long chain-of-thought never floods the viewport (#727, #726)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:66
msgid "Two refinements make expanding predictable:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:68
msgid ""
"**Anchor block on expand**: the clicked block's header is pinned to its "
"screen row, so expanding or collapsing grows the block in place instead of "
"jumping the viewport (#728)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:69
msgid ""
"**Click vs drag on mouse-up**: click-vs-drag is decided on mouse-up, so a "
"click-drag selects text (for copying) instead of toggling the expand state "
"(#726)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:71
msgid "Version in the UI (v0.3.74)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:73
msgid ""
"The running OpenCrabs version now shows on the **TUI header** and in channel "
"`/help` and `/usage` output (#696), so you always know which build a session "
"is on."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:75
msgid "Double-Escape Returns the Query (v0.3.74)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:77
msgid ""
"Pressing `Esc` twice before any reply now **returns the query to the input "
"box and removes it** from the conversation (#698), so a half-typed prompt "
"you cancel doesn't linger as an empty turn."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:79
msgid "Per-Turn Headers (v0.3.75)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:81
msgid ""
"Every turn now gets a **one-line header** summarising the work that turn "
"did, and the turn's working-out folds up into it. OpenCrabs infers turn "
"boundaries so each turn can be grouped, then folds the narration, "
"intermediate text, and tool calls underneath the header."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:83
msgid "The view stays clean by default:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:85
msgid ""
"**Fold every turn by default**: turns fold as soon as they settle (and even "
"while still running), so settled work collapses out of the way instead of "
"scrolling off screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:86
msgid ""
"**Fold live**: intermediate text folds while the turn is still running, and "
"stale narration the model kept thinking past is collapsed."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:87
msgid ""
"**Readable folded turn**: a folded turn stays readable and holds its place "
"when toggled, and the tool-call summary stays at full visibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:88
msgid ""
"**Short live-thinking excerpt**: live thinking shows a short excerpt with "
"room to finish a thought, not a scrolling wall."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:89
msgid ""
"**Labelled token counter**: the live token counter is labelled as a turn "
"total and shows the ctx budget; ctx dropped from the spinner since it "
"already shows under the input."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:91
msgid ""
"Expanding a turn is smooth: the header is kept after expand, and expanding "
"no longer scrolls the view up by its own size."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:93
msgid "TUI Improvements (v0.3.76–v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:95
msgid "Steps AND Tools Display (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:96
msgid ""
"The TUI now shows **both steps and tool calls** in the turn view. Previously "
"it was either/or: if tool calls existed, steps were hidden. Now both render, "
"with steps providing the narrative and tool calls showing the mechanical "
"detail."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:98
msgid "Background Task Position (v0.3.77)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:99
msgid ""
"Background task feedback moved from the **left border to the right border** "
"of the input box. This prevents it from colliding with the context budget "
"footer on the left."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:101
msgid "Duplicate-Submit Guard (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:102
msgid ""
"Pressing Enter twice quickly no longer submits the same message twice. The "
"TUI drops a re-submitted message if the running turn is already answering it."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:104
msgid "Command Labelling (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:105
msgid ""
"Commands in the TUI are now labelled by **what they run** (e.g. \"cargo "
"test\") instead of the working directory. Makes the activity feed readable "
"at a glance."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:107
msgid "Deliverable Report Visibility (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:108
msgid ""
"When a turn produces a deliverable report (audit, comparison, analysis), the "
"report **stays visible** even when the turn folds. Previously, folding a "
"turn would hide the report along with the working-out."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:110
msgid "Background Running Indicator (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:111
msgid ""
"The \"running\" indicator is now **cleared before delivering** the final "
"response. Previously, the indicator could linger for a moment after the "
"response appeared, creating a visual glitch."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:113
msgid "Limits"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/split-panes.md:115
msgid ""
"There is no hard limit on pane count -- you can run as many as your terminal "
"fits. Each pane is a full session with its own token tracking and working "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/dynamic-tools.md:3
msgid ""
"Define custom tools at runtime without recompiling. Tools are defined in "
"`~/.opencrabs/tools.toml` and can be created, removed, and reloaded on the "
