#: src/features/browser.md:3
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs includes native headless Chrome control via the Chrome DevTools "
"Protocol (CDP). No Selenium, no Playwright, direct browser control built "
"into the binary."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:7
msgid "A Chromium-based browser installed (Chrome, Brave, Edge, or Chromium)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:8
msgid "Feature flag: `browser` (enabled by default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:10
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs auto-detects your default Chromium browser, no manual path "
"configuration needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:12
msgid "Browser Tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:19
msgid "Capture a screenshot of the page"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:23
msgid ""
"Find elements matching a pattern (CSS, XPath, text, or aria-label). Returns "
"stable selectors for subsequent click/type operations"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:24
msgid "`browser_act`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:24
msgid ""
"Batched multi-action in one call: an ordered array of `click` / `fill` / "
"`press` / `select` / `wait` / `upload` (max 10 actions, 120s budget). "
"Selectors resolve up front, so a stale reference rejects the whole batch "
"instead of half-running it; aborts on first failure and reports the "
"completed prefix; one screenshot at the end. `upload` attaches local files "
"to a file input without putting their bytes in the context (#2112)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:28
msgid ""
"The browser is lazy-initialized as a singleton, it only launches when the "
"agent first needs it. It runs in stealth mode with a persistent profile "
"directory, so cookies and sessions survive across tool calls."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:30
msgid ""
"On macOS, display auto-detection enables headed mode when a display is "
"available, falling back to headless in CI or daemon environments."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:34 src/features/document-generation.md:49
msgid "Ask the agent:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:36
msgid ""
"\"Go to our staging site, log in with the test account, navigate to the "
"dashboard, and take a screenshot\""
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:38
msgid ""
"The agent will chain `navigate` → `type` (username) → `type` (password) → "
"`click` (login button) → `navigate` (dashboard) → `screenshot`: all "
"autonomously."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:40
msgid "Inventory Mode (v0.3.80)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:42
msgid ""
"`browser_find` now works **without a pattern** (#1022). Call it bare and it "
"enumerates every visible interactive element on the page (links, buttons, "
"inputs, selects, textareas, role=button elements, onclick handlers, tabindex "
"elements, labels, and disclosure widgets) each stamped with a selector and "
"index you can click directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:44
msgid ""
"This is the structural fix for the screenshot-as-discovery loop: instead of "
"screenshotting repeatedly and guessing selectors, the agent gets the page's "
"clickable inventory in one call. When `browser_screenshot` reports an "
"identical page, the hint now nudges toward inventory mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:46
msgid "Shadow-DOM Resolution (v0.5.2)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:48
msgid ""
"Selector resolution is shadow-DOM aware: an element inside one or more "
"shadow roots is reached by piercing the roots along the path, so web "
"components and widget libraries that host their UI in shadow trees are "
"automatable like light-DOM content. Applies across the browser tools (click, "
"type, find, screenshot targeting)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:52
msgid ""
"No configuration needed. The browser feature is enabled by default. To "
"disable it at build time:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/browser.md:55
msgid "\"telegram,discord,slack\""
msgstr ""

