"This conversation's channel (refused on headless surfaces, which have none)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:84
msgid ""
"Target URLs are resolved **once, at create/update time**, and the concrete "
"channel target is baked into the job; if an unbaked URL ever reaches fire "
"time the run fails loudly instead of resolving against a possibly-changed "
"world."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:88
msgid "Forum-topic delivery (v0.5.1, opt-in)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:90
msgid ""
"`telegram:CHAT_ID:THREAD_ID` (or the `oc://telegram/<chat>/<thread>` form) "
"delivers into a specific topic of a forum group. It is deliberately opt-in: "
"the chat must actually be a forum and the topic must exist: an invalid "
"thread target is **rejected loudly at fire time**, never silently re-routed "
"to the general topic. When a job is created from inside a thread "
"(`here`/`oc://` form), the origin thread id is persisted so the result lands "
"back in the same topic (#104)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:97
msgid ""
"Results are stored in the DB via the `cron_results` table regardless of "
"delivery target, so you can query past execution results with `opencrabs "
"cron results <name>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:99
msgid "Trigger-gated jobs (v0.5.3)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:101
msgid ""
"A job can carry a **pre-flight trigger**: at each fire time the scheduler "
"runs a shell command first, and only executes the prompt when a condition on "
"that command's result is met. This turns scheduled jobs from \"fires into "
"the void every hour\" into \"acts when something actually happened\" (a file "
"appeared, a health check failed, a log line matched) (#233)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:107
msgid "Set it through the `cron_manage` tool at create or update time:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:111
msgid "`trigger_cmd`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:111
msgid ""
"Shell command run under `/bin/sh -c` before the prompt. 30s timeout; a hung "
"trigger is killed, not orphaned. Either `prompt` or `trigger_cmd` must be "
"set."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:112
msgid "`trigger_on`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:112
msgid "Fire condition (see below). Default `non_empty`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:113
msgid "`set_goal`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:113
msgid ""
"On fire, set the active goal in the destination session instead of a plain "
"prompt turn. Requires `deliver_to` to target a session; refused for passive "
"channel deliveries."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:114
msgid "`goal_template`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:114
msgid ""
"Template for the goal/notification text. Interpolates `{output}`, "
"`{stdout}`, `{stderr}`, `{exit_code}`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:116
msgid "`trigger_on` conditions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:118 src/features/rtk.md:20
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:118
msgid "Fires when"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:120
msgid "`non_empty` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:120
msgid "stdout or stderr contains any non-whitespace output"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:121
msgid "`exit_zero`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:121
msgid "the trigger exits 0"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:122
msgid "`exit_non_zero`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:122
msgid "the trigger exits non-zero (health checks, `grep` misses)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:123
msgid "`regex:PATTERN` or `re:PATTERN`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:123
msgid "combined output matches the regular expression"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:124
msgid "`always`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:124
msgid "the trigger finished, regardless of output or exit code"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:126
msgid "Semantics"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:128
msgid ""
"**Condition not met** → the run is short-circuited at 0 tokens and recorded "
"as a skipped/success run. The prompt never executes, nothing is delivered."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:130
msgid ""
"**Trigger command errors or times out** → the run is recorded as an error; "
"the prompt still does not execute."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:132
msgid ""
"**Empty `prompt` with a trigger** → direct 0-token delivery: the formatted "
"trigger output (`goal_template`, or the raw output) is delivered to "
"`deliver_to` without an agent turn at all."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:135
msgid ""
"**`set_goal`** → the fired trigger dispatches into the target session as an "
"active goal, so the session's agent works the condition it detected rather "
"than just echoing output."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:139
msgid ""
"Put the watching in `trigger_cmd` (deterministic, cheap, script-runner "
"pattern), the condition in `trigger_on`, and the acting in the prompt or "
"goal."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:142
msgid "Scheduler Lock (v0.3.65)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/cron-jobs.md:144
msgid ""
"The cron scheduler uses a **file lock** to prevent duplicate job execution. "
"Only one scheduler instance can run per profile at a time. If you "
"accidentally start OpenCrabs twice, the second instance won't fire duplicate "
"cron jobs."
msgstr ""

