#: src/features/plans.md:3
msgid ""
"Plans provide structured multi-step task execution with a live progress "
"widget in the TUI."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:5
msgid "Creating a Plan"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:7
msgid "Ask the agent to plan a complex task:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:9
msgid ""
"```\n"
"\"Plan the migration from PostgreSQL to SQLite\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:13
msgid "The agent uses the `plan` tool internally to create a plan with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:14
msgid "Title and description"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:15
msgid "Technical stack"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:16
msgid "Risk assessment"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:17
msgid "Test strategy"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:18
msgid "Ordered tasks with dependencies and complexity ratings"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:20
msgid "Plan Lifecycle"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:22
msgid "**Draft**: Agent creates the plan and adds tasks"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:23
msgid ""
"**Finalize**: Agent calls `finalize` which triggers the tool approval dialog"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:24
msgid ""
"**Approved**: You approve in the tool dialog, plan status becomes "
"`Approved`, and the agent begins executing tasks immediately"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:25
msgid "**In Progress**: Tasks execute in dependency order"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:26
msgid "**Completed**: All tasks done"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:28
msgid ""
"In **ask mode** (default), the `finalize` step triggers the tool approval "
"dialog, you review the full plan before execution begins. In **auto-approve "
"mode**, finalize is auto-approved and the agent plans and executes without "
"pausing."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:30
msgid "Plan Requirement Gate"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:32
msgid ""
"A turn that crosses a threshold of tool calls has to stop and write a plan "
"before it continues (#2128). This is what keeps a sprawling refactor from "
"being discovered after twenty files have already changed: you see the shape "
"of the work, and you get a chance to say no before it lands."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:34
msgid ""
"The gate is configurable under `[agent]`. A turn that already has a live "
"plan is never gated again, and a session configured to run autonomously is "
"not stalled by an approval prompt it was told to skip."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:36
msgid "Task States"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:38
msgid "Each task in a plan can be:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:39
msgid "`Pending` (·): Waiting for dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:40
msgid "`InProgress` (▶): Currently executing"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:41
msgid "`Completed` (✓): Done"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:42
msgid "`Skipped` (✓): Manually skipped"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:43
msgid "`Failed` (✗): Execution failed"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:44
msgid "`Blocked` (·): Dependencies not met"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:46
msgid "TUI Plan Widget"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:48
msgid ""
"When a plan is active, a live checklist panel appears above the input box "
"showing:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:50
msgid "**Plan title** and progress counter (e.g. `3/7`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:51
msgid "**Progress bar**: Visual `██████░░░░` bar with percentage"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:52
msgid "**Task list**: Up to 6 tasks visible with status icons and task numbers"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:53
msgid ""
"**Overflow indicator**: `... (N more)` when tasks exceed the visible limit"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:55
msgid "The widget updates in real-time as the agent completes each task."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:57
msgid "Managing Plans"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:59
msgid "Plans are managed through natural language:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:61
msgid ""
"```\n"
"\"Approve the plan\"\n"
"\"Reject the plan\"\n"
"\"What's the plan status?\"\n"
"\"Skip task 3\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:68
msgid ""
"The agent handles plan creation, approval, execution, and status reporting "
"through the `plan` tool."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:70
msgid "Mid-Plan Insertion (v0.3.36)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:72
msgid ""
"Tasks can be inserted at any position in an existing plan using "
"`insert_after`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:74
msgid ""
"```\n"
"plan(operation: \"add_task\", insert_after: 3, title: \"Re-run tests after "
"fix\", ...)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:78
msgid ""
"This inserts the new task as task #4, and all existing tasks from #4 onward "
"are **renumbered automatically**. Dependencies between tasks are preserved "
"through the renumber."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:80
msgid ""
"This is useful when a later task introduces a bug caught by an earlier test. "
"Instead of re-opening the completed test task, insert a fresh re-test task "
"right after the fix."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:82
msgid "Finished Checklist Persistence (v0.3.76)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:84
msgid ""
"When a plan completes all tasks, the finished checklist now **stays on "
"screen** instead of disappearing. You can review the final state (all tasks "
"marked ✓) without having to ask \"what was the plan?\" again. The completed "
"card renders its final state with the full task list and progress bar at "
"100%."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:86
msgid "Epistemic Orient Gate (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:88
msgid ""
"Plan execution is now gated behind an **epistemic Orient phase** before any "
"task starts. The agent must:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:90
msgid "**Observe**: gather ground truth (read files, check state)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:91
msgid "**Orient**: map observations against current beliefs and goals"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:92
msgid "**Decide**: form intention, confirm alignment and safety"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:93
msgid "**Act**: execute through mechanical gates"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:95
msgid ""
"This prevents the agent from charging into a plan task with stale "
"assumptions. The Orient gate checks whether the agent's beliefs about the "
"codebase/state still hold before writing anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:97
msgid "Criteria-Aware Verification (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:99
msgid ""
"The Ralph loop (OpenCrabs' iterative task execution engine) now verifies "
"task completion against **declared acceptance criteria** instead of just "
"\"did the command exit 0?\". Each task's criteria are checked mechanically:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:101
msgid ""
"If a task declares `acceptance_criteria`, the verification gate checks each "
"one"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:102
msgid ""
"Criteria that require specific output (e.g. \"clippy passes with zero "
"warnings\") are verified against actual tool output"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:103
msgid "Tasks without explicit criteria fall back to the standard exit-code check"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:105
msgid ""
"This means a task marked \"complete\" actually met its stated goals, not "
"just \"something ran.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:107
msgid "Ralph Verification Gate + Iteration Cap (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:109
msgid ""
"The Ralph loop gained a **mechanical verification gate** with an iteration "
"cap:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:111
msgid ""
"After each task execution, the gate checks whether the outcome matches the "
"intention"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:112
msgid "If verification fails, the task retries (up to the iteration cap)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:113
msgid ""
"The cap prevents infinite loops on tasks that can never satisfy their "
"criteria"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:114
msgid ""
"State lives in files, not context, each iteration reads fresh state from disk"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:116
msgid ""
"Combined with the epistemic Orient gate, this makes plan execution "
"significantly more reliable: the agent orients before acting, and verifies "
"after acting, with bounded retries."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:118
msgid "Plan State Across Sessions (v0.3.79)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:120
msgid ""
"Plans are no longer tied to the lifetime of a single session. Plan state "
"threads across session boundaries, so a plan survives session swaps, "
"restarts, and context compaction. Spawned child sessions resolve their "
"parent's plan file automatically, which is what makes the next feature "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:122
msgid "Isolated Plan-Task Execution"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:124
msgid ""
"Each plan task can now run in a **freshly spawned isolated worker session**: "
"the worker gets only the task brief and the plan file, not the parent "
"conversation's context. The brief is self-contained and the worker reports "
"its verdict back via disk, so nothing leaks between the parent session and "
"the task, and a long-running task can't burn the parent's context window."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:126
msgid ""
"`agent.plan_isolated_execution` is the master switch, and it **defaults ON** "
"since v0.3.79: Ralph loops run fresh-context by construction, so isolation "
"is the only sane default for autonomous execution."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:127
msgid ""
"An explicit `isolated: true/false` on a `start` call still wins over the "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:128
msgid ""
"Ralph verification now runs in the **session's own working directory**, not "
"the directory OpenCrabs was launched from, a plan in one repo is verified "
"against that repo's build results, not another repo's (#921)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:129
msgid ""
"The plan gate's `RequireApproval` decision respects `auto_approve`, so "
"autonomous sessions are not stalled by an approval prompt they were "
"configured to skip (#934)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:131
msgid "Type-Aware Verification (v0.3.83)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:133
msgid ""
"Acceptance criteria are **checked against the plan's toolchain** (#1133): a "
"Rust task must satisfy cargo-shaped criteria, a Flutter task flutter-shaped "
"ones, and a task whose criteria cannot be verified is marked instead of "
"waved through. Plans also **verify with the project's own toolchain** rather "
"than always cargo, and locate the project from the folder the session is "
"working in. Checklist plans no longer write a design scaffold `.md` (#1145)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:135
msgid "Importing Pre-Defined Plans (v0.3.35)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:137
msgid "Plans can be loaded from JSON files for repeatable workflows:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:139
msgid ""
"```\n"
"plan(operation: \"import\", file_path: \"~/plans/rust-refactor.json\")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:143
msgid ""
"Bundled reference plans ship with OpenCrabs at "
"`~/.opencrabs/profiles/<profile>/plans/` covering common patterns like "
"`rust-fast`, `rust-medium`, `rust-full`, `python-fast`, `python-medium`, "
"`python-full`, and `sample-minimal-plan`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:145
msgid ""
"The JSON format requires a minimum of 6 fields: `title`, `description`, plus "
"3 fields per task (`title`, `description`, `task_type`). Full schema "
"supports dependencies, complexity ratings, acceptance criteria, and "
"technical stack."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/plans.md:147
msgid ""
"**Security:** Import validates symlinks against the target path only "
"(rejecting ancestor false positives on macOS) and checks for orphan "
"dependencies that reference non-existent tasks."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:3
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs supports spawning specialized sub-agents that run autonomously in "
"isolated sessions. Each child agent gets its own context, tool registry, and "
"cancel token. Introduced in **v0.2.97** with a typed agent system and team "
"orchestration."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:7
msgid ""
"When spawning an agent, an `agent_type` parameter selects a specialized role "
"with a curated tool set:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:11
msgid "Full-capability agent (default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:12
msgid "Fast codebase navigation (read-only)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:13
msgid "Architecture planning (read + analysis)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:14
msgid "Implementation (full write access)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:17
msgid ""
"Each type receives a role-specific system prompt that shapes its behavior. "
"Explore agents are fast and lightweight -- they only read files. Code agents "
"can modify anything. Research agents can search the web but not touch your "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:19
msgid "Safety: ALWAYS_EXCLUDED Tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:21
msgid ""
"No agent type has access to these tools, preventing dangerous or recursive "
"operations:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:23
msgid "`spawn_agent` -- no spawning agents from agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:24
msgid ""
"`resume_agent`, `wait_agent`, `send_input`, `close_agent` -- no managing "
"siblings"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:25
msgid "`rebuild` -- no building from source"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:26
msgid "`evolve` -- no self-updating"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:28
msgid "Five Orchestration Tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:32
msgid ""
"Create a typed child agent to handle a sub-task autonomously in the "
"background"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:33
msgid ""
"Wait for a spawned agent to complete and return its output (configurable "
"timeout)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:34
msgid "Send follow-up instructions to a running agent (multi-turn conversation)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:35
msgid "Terminate a running agent and clean up its resources"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:36
msgid ""
"Resume a completed or failed agent with a new prompt (preserves prior "
"context)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:38
msgid "Spawn an Agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:40
msgid ""
"```\n"
"spawn_agent(\n"
"  label: \"refactor-auth\",      # Human-readable label\n"
"  agent_type: \"code\",          # general | explore | plan | code | "
"research\n"
"  prompt: \"Refactor auth...\",  # Task instruction\n"
"  include_brain: false         # opt in to workspace brain pre-injection "
"(v0.5.1)\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:49
msgid ""
"The agent runs in its own session with auto-approved tools. No blocking -- "
"it executes in the background while the parent continues."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:51
msgid "Lean children and `include_brain` (v0.5.1)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:53
msgid ""
"Sub-agents start **lean**: no pre-injected workspace brain (SOUL.md, "
"USER.md, AGENTS.md, project directives). Pass `include_brain: true` to "
"`spawn_agent` (or per-agent in `team_create`) to opt into pre-injection; the "
"choice is frozen for the agent's lifetime and `resume_agent` re-attaches "
"accordingly. When a child runs lean, its prompt **discloses the gap**: the "
"child is told the workspace brain is not loaded and pointed at "
"`load_brain_file` for on-demand access, so neither side operates on the "
"assumption rules are ambiently known (#145)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:60
msgid "Headless children (v0.5.1)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:62
msgid ""
"Child agents are **headless by law**: interactive-only tools "
"(`session_notify`, `suggest_options`) are stripped from the child's tool "
"surface and the registry refuses to register them there: a call returns a "
"hard tool error, not a silent no-op. The headless tool roster excludes "
"interactive-only tools wholesale, and headless prompts (spawn and resume, "
"cron/daemon, CLI one-shot) carry a preamble saying so, so the child never "
"reaches for a button it does not have (#129). The same backstop covers "
"cron's `here` target: it is refused on headless surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:70
msgid "Wait for Completion"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:72
msgid ""
"```\n"
"wait_agent(\n"
"  agent_id: \"abc-123\",\n"
"  timeout_secs: 300            # Max wait time (default: 300s)\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:79
msgid "Multi-Turn with send_input"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:81
msgid "After spawning, you can send additional instructions without restarting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:83
msgid ""
"```\n"
"send_input(\n"
"  agent_id: \"abc-123\",\n"
"  text: \"Also add unit tests for the new module\"\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:90
msgid ""
"The child agent processes the input on its next iteration. This enables "
"iterative workflows -- review the agent's output, then ask it to refine or "
"continue."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:92
msgid "Resume a Completed Agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:94
msgid ""
"```\n"
"resume_agent(\n"
"  agent_id: \"abc-123\",\n"
"  prompt: \"Now port the same changes to the other two files\"\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:101
msgid ""
"The agent continues in its original session, preserving all prior context. "
"No need to re-explain the codebase."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:103
msgid "Team Orchestration"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:105
msgid ""
"The `TeamManager` coordinates named groups of agents for parallel execution. "
"Three team-specific tools:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:107
msgid "Create a Team"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:109
msgid ""
"```\n"
"team_create(\n"
"  team_name: \"backend-refactor\",\n"
"  agents: [\n"
"    { label: \"auth\", agent_type: \"code\", prompt: \"Refactor auth "
"module\" },\n"
"    { label: \"tests\", agent_type: \"code\", prompt: \"Write tests for "
"auth\" },\n"
"    { label: \"docs\", agent_type: \"general\", prompt: \"Update "
"documentation\" }\n"
"  ]\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:120
msgid ""
"All agents spawn simultaneously and run in parallel. Returns the team name "
"and all agent IDs."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:122
msgid "Broadcast to a Team"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:124
msgid ""
"```\n"
"team_broadcast(\n"
"  team_name: \"backend-refactor\",\n"
"  message: \"Use the new AuthError enum instead of plain strings\"\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:131
msgid ""
"Sends a message to all running agents in the team. Non-running agents are "
"skipped. Useful for sharing context or direction changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:133
msgid "Delete a Team"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:135
msgid ""
"```\n"
"team_delete(team_name: \"backend-refactor\")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:139
msgid ""
"Cancels all running agents and cleans up resources. Completed agents are "
"left in the subagent manager for reference."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:141
msgid "Subagent Provider/Model Config"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:143
msgid ""
"By default, every spawned agent inherits the parent session's provider and "
"model. You can override this globally in `config.toml` so child agents route "
"to a different (usually cheaper or faster) backend:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:145
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[agent]\n"
"subagent_provider = \"openrouter\"   # Provider for child agents\n"
"subagent_model    = \"qwen/qwen3-235b\" # Model override\n"
"\n"
"# Omit both keys and child agents inherit the parent session's provider\n"
"# and run on that provider's default model.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:154
msgid ""
"The override applies to `spawn_agent`, `resume_agent`, and every member of a "
"`team_create` team. Changes take effect on next session start; running "
"sessions keep their existing provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:156
msgid "Per-Call Overrides (v0.3.35)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:158
msgid ""
"`spawn_agent`, `resume_agent`, and `team_create` now accept optional "
"`provider` and `model` fields that override config defaults for a single "
"call. This enables mixed-model teams:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:160
msgid ""
"```\n"
"team_create(\n"
"  team_name: \"mixed-stack\",\n"
"  agents: [\n"
"    { label: \"planner\", provider: \"zhipu\", model: \"glm-5\", prompt: "
"\"Architect the feature\" },\n"
"    { label: \"coder\", provider: \"deepseek\", model: \"deepseek-coder\", "
"prompt: \"Implement it\" },\n"
"    { label: \"reviewer\", provider: \"kimi\", model: \"kimi-k2.5\", prompt: "
"\"Review the code\" }\n"
"  ]\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:171
msgid ""
"Precedence order (highest first): per-call `provider`/`model` > `[agent] "
"subagent_provider`/`subagent_model` in config > parent session's provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:173 src/features/rtk.md:126
msgid "Why It Matters"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:175
msgid ""
"The common pattern is **premium parent, cheap children**. Your main "
"conversation stays on a reasoning-capable model (Opus, GPT-5, Gemini 2.5 "
"Pro) while subtasks (file exploration, test writing, web research, bulk "
"refactors) run on a faster, cheaper model. With a 4-agent team running 10 "
"minutes each, the cost delta between Opus and Qwen on the children is "
"roughly 50x."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:177
msgid "Concrete Examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:179
msgid ""
"**OpenRouter parent, Qwen children**, best bang-for-buck on mixed workloads:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:180
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.openrouter]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"api_key = \"sk-or-...\"\n"
"model = \"anthropic/claude-opus-4\"\n"
"\n"
"[agent]\n"
"subagent_provider = \"openrouter\"\n"
"subagent_model    = \"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:191
msgid ""
"**Kimi on custom OpenCode provider**: fast code generation for `code` and "
"`explore` agents:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:192
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.opencode-kimi]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"base_url = \"https://api.kimi.com/v1\"\n"
"api_key  = \"...\"\n"
"model    = \"kimi-k2.5\"\n"
"\n"
"[agent]\n"
"subagent_provider = \"opencode-kimi\"\n"
"subagent_model    = \"kimi-k2.6\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:204
msgid ""
"**Local Ollama children**: zero cost, fully offline, good for `explore` "
"agents that just read files:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:205
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.ollama]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"model = \"qwen3:14b\"\n"
"\n"
"[agent]\n"
"subagent_provider = \"ollama\"\n"
"subagent_model    = \"qwen3:14b\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:215
msgid ""
"**Gemini parent, Gemini Flash children**, single billing account, reasoning "
"on main, flash on team:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:216
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.gemini]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"model = \"gemini-2.5-pro\"\n"
"\n"
"[agent]\n"
"subagent_provider = \"gemini\"\n"
"subagent_model    = \"gemini-2.5-flash\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:226
msgid "Gotchas"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:228
msgid ""
"The subagent provider must be enabled and have a valid API key (or be a "
"CLI/none-auth provider). Missing keys cause the spawn to fail with a "
"provider resolution error."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:229
msgid ""
"`subagent_model` must be a model the provider actually serves. "
"`qwen/qwen3-235b` works on OpenRouter, not on Anthropic. Check `/models` on "
"the target provider to confirm."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:230
msgid ""
"`team_create` members all share the same subagent config. If you need "
"heterogeneous routing (e.g. a research agent on web-search model, a code "
"agent on code-specialized model), spawn them individually with `spawn_agent` "
"under different config profiles."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:231
msgid ""
"The CLI model override is surfaced in the `spawn_agent`, `resume_agent`, and "
"`team_create` tool descriptions themselves, so the LLM knows to mention "
"these keys to you instead of inventing per-call overrides."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:233
msgid ""
"If `subagent_provider` or `subagent_model` is not set, the spawned agent "
"loads from the parent session's provider and runs on that provider's default "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:235
msgid "Workflow Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:237
msgid "Parallel Research + Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:239
msgid ""
"```\n"
"team_create(\"feature-research\", [\n"
"  { label: \"research\", agent_type: \"research\", prompt: \"Find best "
"practices for rate limiting in Rust\" },\n"
"  { label: \"explore\", agent_type: \"explore\", prompt: \"Find all "
"middleware files in the codebase\" }\n"
"])\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:246
msgid "Wait for results, then spawn a code agent with the combined context."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:248
msgid "Iterative Code Review"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:250
msgid ""
"```\n"
"# 1. Spawn a code agent\n"
"spawn_agent(label: \"impl\", agent_type: \"code\", prompt: \"Implement rate "
"limiting middleware\")\n"
"\n"
"# 2. Wait for completion\n"
"wait_agent(agent_id: \"impl-id\")\n"
"\n"
"# 3. Resume with refinements\n"
"resume_agent(agent_id: \"impl-id\", prompt: \"Add tests for the edge cases "
"we discussed\")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:261
msgid "Large-Scale Refactoring"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:263
msgid ""
"```\n"
"team_create(\"refactor-team\", [\n"
"  { label: \"module-a\", agent_type: \"code\", prompt: \"Refactor module A "
"to use the new trait\" },\n"
"  { label: \"module-b\", agent_type: \"code\", prompt: \"Refactor module B "
"to use the new trait\" },\n"
"  { label: \"module-c\", agent_type: \"code\", prompt: \"Refactor module C "
"to use the new trait\" },\n"
"  { label: \"tests\", agent_type: \"code\", prompt: \"Update all tests for "
"the new trait signature\" }\n"
"])\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

