msgid "Manager state machine (spawn, wait, close lifecycle)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:276
msgid "`SendInput` wiring and input loop"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:277
msgid "`CloseAgent` cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:278
msgid "`WaitAgent` timeout behavior"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:279
msgid "`AgentType` tool filtering"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:280
msgid "`TeamManager`, `TeamDelete`, `TeamBroadcast`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:281
msgid "Registry exclusion (ALWAYS_EXCLUDED enforcement)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:283
msgid "Sub-Agent Result Reporting (v0.3.81)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:285
msgid ""
"A finished agent **reports its result back to the spawning session** "
"(#1036): the parent sees the outcome in-turn instead of polling or reading "
"status files. Orphaned sub-agent status files from crashed runs are "
"**reconciled at startup** (#1038), so the registry never shows ghosts of "
"agents that no longer exist."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:287
msgid "Sub-Agent Worktree Isolation (v0.3.83)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/multi-agent.md:289
msgid ""
"Each spawned agent gets **its own worktree and branch** instead of sharing "
"the parent's working tree: a fan-out of several agents on one repository can "
"no longer clobber each other's checkouts or builds. The parent's tree stays "
"untouched while children work in isolation, and results come back through "
"the normal git flow."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/a2a.md:1
msgid "Agent-to-Agent (A2A) Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/a2a.md:3
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs includes a built-in A2A gateway implementing the [A2A Protocol RC "
"v1.0](https://google.github.io/A2A/) for peer-to-peer agent communication."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/a2a.md:5
msgid "Enabling"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/a2a.md:7
msgid ""
"**Legacy `[gateway]` name (v0.3.82):** this section was once spelled "
"`[gateway]`. Both spellings now fold into one setting, and the legacy name "
"is **rewritten to `[a2a]` on disk** so it survives a reload round trip "
"instead of reappearing (#1116). Nothing to do by hand; an existing "
"`[gateway]` block migrates itself on the next load."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/a2a.md:9
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# config.toml\n"
"[a2a]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"bind = \"127.0.0.1\"   # Loopback only (default): use \"0.0.0.0\" to expose "
"externally\n"
"port = 18790\n"
"# api_key = \"your-secret\"  # Optional Bearer token auth for incoming "
"requests\n"
"# allowed_origins = [\"http://localhost:3000\"]  # CORS\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

