#: src/features/acp.md:3
msgid ""
"**ACP server mode** lets agent-aware editors (Zed, MonoCode, any ACP client) "
"drive OpenCrabs as a backend agent over the [Agent Client "
"Protocol](https://agentclientprotocol.com). The editor spawns `opencrabs "
"acp` as a child process and speaks JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, so your editor "
"session and your channels share the same brain, tools, memory, and provider "
"configuration (#1540)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:5
msgid "Running"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:8
msgid "# default model from config\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:12
msgid ""
"Point your editor's ACP/agent client at the `opencrabs acp` command and it "
"appears as an available agent. One child process serves one conversation "
"thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:16
msgid "**Framing**: JSON-RPC 2.0, newline-delimited (NDJSON) over stdio"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:17
msgid ""
"**`session/prompt`**: runs the full tool loop for a turn; the reply arrives "
"when the turn settles"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:18
msgid ""
"**`session/update`**: progress notifications stream back while the turn "
"works (tool calls, output chunks)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:19
msgid ""
"**`session/request_permission`**: tool approvals round-trip to the editor, "
"so the client's permission UI gates dangerous calls the same way channel "
"approvals do"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:21
msgid ""
"stdout is the protocol channel: nothing but JSON-RPC frames is ever written "
"to it. Logs go to the daily log file (or stderr in debug builds), never "
"stdout."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:23
msgid "Sessions (v0.5.4)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:25
msgid "Sessions are first-class on the ACP surface:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:27
msgid ""
"**`session/new`** offers a live model catalog, so the client picks from "
"models that actually exist in your config"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:28
msgid ""
"**`session/load`** replays the transcript and restores the per-session model"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:29
msgid "**`set_model`** persists on the session row and survives process restarts"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:30
msgid ""
"**`session/set_mode`** applies the approval policy server-side (native, no "
"prompt workaround)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:31
msgid "**`session/compact`** pushes compaction to the client"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:32
msgid ""
"The context meter is restored on load and rides usage updates, so the editor "
"always shows a true context reading"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:34
msgid "Session Lifecycle v1 (v0.5.5)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:36
msgid ""
"The ACP server now implements the five v1 session lifecycle methods (#1815): "
"`session/list` pages your sessions with a cursor, `session/resume` "
"reattaches without replaying history while still restoring the model pin, "
"`session/set_config_option` is the write half of the model picker (F4 only "
"displayed it before), `session/close` cancels in-flight work and frees live "
"state, and `session/delete` removes the row after freeing it. `initialize` "
"now advertises the list, resume, close, and delete session capabilities. The "
"plan is also published as a native v1 plan update, and image prompt blocks "
"sent by the client are decoded into `<<IMG>>` attachments the agent can "
"actually see."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:38
msgid "Why it matters"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/acp.md:40
msgid ""
"Before ACP mode, driving OpenCrabs from an editor meant copy-pasting between "
"the editor and a channel. With ACP mode the editor is a first-class surface: "
"same providers, same skill gating, same plan approvals, same memory. "
"Configuration is shared with the rest of OpenCrabs; there is no separate ACP "
"config section."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:3
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs monitors its own health and automatically recovers from failures "
"without user intervention. All recovery events surface as visible "
"notifications across TUI and all channels."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:5
msgid "How It Differs from Crash Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:7
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs has had **crash recovery** since early versions -- if the process "
"dies mid-request, pending requests are tracked in SQLite and automatically "
"resumed on restart (see [Pending Request "
"Recovery](#pending-request-recovery) below)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:9
msgid ""
"**Self-healing** (v0.2.92) goes further: the agent detects and fixes "
"problems _while it's still running_ -- corrupted config, degraded providers, "
"context overflow, stuck streams, DB corruption -- without restarting. Crash "
"recovery is the safety net; self-healing prevents the fall."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:11
msgid "Config Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:13
msgid ""
"Every successful write to `config.toml` creates a snapshot at "
"`~/.opencrabs/config.last_good.toml`. When the config becomes corrupted or "
"unparseable, OpenCrabs restores from the last-known-good snapshot "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:19
msgid ""
"A `CONFIG_RECOVERED` atomic flag tracks whether recovery happened during the "
"current session, so downstream code can react accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:21
msgid "Unknown Key Detection"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:23
msgid ""
"Unknown top-level keys in `config.toml` trigger a startup warning listing "
"the unrecognized entries. This catches typos like `[teelgram]` or "
"`[a2a_gatway]` before they cause silent misconfiguration."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:25
msgid ""
"Known valid sections: `[crabrace]`, `[database]`, `[logging]`, `[debug]`, "
"`[providers]`, `[channels]`, `[agent]`, `[daemon]`, `[a2a]`, `[image]`, "
"`[cron]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:27
msgid ""
"The `[a2a]` section also accepts `gateway` as an alias via serde, "
"deduplicating a common typo."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:29
msgid "Custom Provider Name Normalization"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:31
msgid ""
"Provider names with mixed case or whitespace (e.g. `\"My Provider\"` vs "
"`\"my provider\"`) are normalized on load and save, preventing duplicate "
"entries that would confuse the provider registry."
msgstr ""

