msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:71
msgid "Pane state persistence"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:73
msgid ""
"**Before:** `let _ = ...` and `.ok()` everywhere, errors vanish. **After:** "
"Every error surfaces via logging or user notification."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:76
msgid ""
"Onboarding config writes use `try_write!` macros that batch errors during "
"wizard steps and report them all at the end, so users see exactly what "
"failed."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:78
msgid "AgentService Config Propagation"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:80
msgid ""
"`AgentService::new()` now requires an explicit `&Config` parameter instead "
"of calling `Config::load()` internally. This eliminates hidden I/O, makes "
"dependencies explicit, and enables test injection via "
"`AgentService::new_for_test()`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:82
msgid ""
"Render, dialogs, messaging, and cron modules no longer call `Config::load()` "
"internally -- errors propagate up the call stack instead of being swallowed."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:84
msgid "Context Budget Management"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:86
msgid ""
"The agent enforces a **65% context budget threshold**. When token usage "
"reaches 65% of the effective context window (context limit minus tool schema "
"overhead), automatic LLM compaction fires:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:88
msgid "**Detect** context usage ≥ 65% of effective max tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:89
msgid ""
"**Compact** via LLM summarization (preserves meaning, not just truncation)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:90
msgid "**Retry** up to 3 times if compaction fails"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:91
msgid "**Second pass** with tighter budget if still over threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:93
msgid ""
"The 65% threshold exists because providers like MiniMax degrade on "
"function-calling quality well before hitting theoretical context limits -- "
"tool calls break around ~133k tokens of a 200k limit."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:95
msgid "Async Proactive Compaction (v0.3.16)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:97
msgid ""
"At 65% context, compaction now runs **asynchronously in the background** "
"instead of blocking the chat. The agent continues processing while the LLM "
"summarizes older messages. Once compaction completes, the context is swapped "
"seamlessly. No more frozen UI during compaction."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:99
msgid "**Source:** `src/brain/agent/service/tool_loop.rs` (lines 14-112)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:101
msgid "Emergency Compaction (ARG_MAX Recovery)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:103
msgid ""
"When CLI provider conversation context exceeds the OS `ARG_MAX` limit (~1MB "
"on macOS), the agent recovers with a 3-stage fallback:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:105
msgid "**Catch** the \"Argument list too long\" or \"prompt too large\" error"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:106
msgid "**Emergency compact** the conversation with an LLM summarization pass"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:107
msgid "**Insert** a system marker so the agent knows context was compacted"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:108
msgid "**Retry** the request"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:110
msgid ""
"If compaction still fails, **hard truncation** kicks in -- keeps last 24 "
"messages (12 conversation pairs) with a marker telling the agent to use "
"`search_session` for older context. Both markers persist to DB for recovery "
"across sessions."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:112
msgid ""
"Both actions emit `SelfHealingAlert` progress events so users see exactly "
"what happened."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:114
msgid ""
"**Source:** `src/brain/agent/service/tool_loop.rs` (lines 550-687), tested "
"with `ArgTooLongMockProvider` and `ContextLengthMockProvider` in "
"`src/tests/cli_arg_too_long_test.rs` (352 lines)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:116
msgid "Stream Resilience"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:118
msgid "Stuck Loop Detection"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:120
msgid ""
"Some streaming providers (notably MiniMax) occasionally loop the same "
"content indefinitely without sending a stop signal. The agent detects this:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:122
msgid "Maintains a **2048-byte rolling window** of recent streamed text"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:123
msgid ""
"When a **200+ byte substring** from the second half appears in the first "
"half, it's a repeat"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:124
msgid "Stream is terminated immediately and retry logic fires"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:126
msgid ""
"**Source:** `src/brain/agent/service/helpers.rs` -- "
"`detect_text_repetition()`, tested in `src/tests/stream_loop_test.rs` (15 "
"tests)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:128
msgid "Idle Timeout"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:130
msgid ""
"If a stream goes silent for **60 seconds** (API providers) or **10 minutes** "
"(CLI providers) with no events, it's treated as a dropped connection."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:132
msgid ""
"CLI providers (Claude CLI, OpenCode CLI) run internal tools (cargo builds, "
"tests, `gh` commands) that can take several minutes without producing stream "
"events. The 60-second timeout caused premature termination on these, so CLI "
"providers now get a 10-minute window before timeout fires."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:134
msgid "If a stream goes silent:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:140
msgid ""
"The `tokio::select!` loop races the stream against the timeout and the "
"user's cancellation token. Timeout triggers retry, not a hard error."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:142
msgid "Pending Request Recovery"
