msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:183
msgid "Cached pane state (stale split pane entries)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:185
msgid ""
"Custom provider names are **normalized** on load and save (`\"My Provider\"` "
"→ `\"my-provider\"`), preventing duplicate entries that would confuse the "
"provider registry."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:187
msgid "Model Selector Safety"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:189
msgid ""
"Pressing Enter in the model selector no longer clears existing API keys. The "
"selector preserves current configuration while switching models."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:191
msgid ""
"Model switching errors now surface the actual error with a `⚠️` prefix on "
"all channels, instead of always showing \"Model switched\" even on failure."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:193
msgid "UTF-8 Safety"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:195
msgid ""
"`split_message()` across all 5 channel handlers (Telegram, Discord, Slack, "
"WhatsApp, Trello) now uses `is_char_boundary()` to find safe split points, "
"preventing panics on multi-byte characters (emojis, CJK, accented "
"characters)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:197
msgid "Cancel Persistence (v0.2.97)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:199
msgid ""
"When a user double-Escapes to abort a streaming response, the partial "
"content is now **persisted to the database before `handle.abort()` fires**. "
"This means cancelled content survives a session reload -- you can scroll "
"back and see exactly what the agent was saying before you stopped it."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:201
msgid "Claude CLI Subprocess Cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:203
msgid ""
"Previously, aborting a Claude CLI request would orphan the underlying "
"`claude` subprocess. Now the stream reader loop monitors `tx.closed()` via "
"`tokio::select!` and kills the child process when the receiver drops, "
"preventing leaked subprocesses accumulating in the background."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:205
msgid "Telegram Stale Delivery Suppression"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:207
msgid ""
"When a request is cancelled mid-flight, the agent sometimes continued "
"processing and delivered a stale response to Telegram. A "
"`cancel_token.is_cancelled()` guard now fires before final delivery, "
"preventing old agent results from posting after cancellation."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:209
msgid "Config Overwrite Protection"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:211
msgid ""
"The onboarding wizard previously overwrote existing channel settings on "
"every save, causing data loss when re-running `/onboard`. `apply_config()` "
"now scopes writes to only the current onboarding step. `from_config()` sets "
"`EXISTING_KEY_SENTINEL` for all existing channel data, ensuring untouched "
"fields are never overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:213
msgid "Tool Description Wrapping"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:215
msgid ""
"Tool call descriptions were previously truncated at 80 characters in the "
"TUI. `render_tool_group` now **wraps** description headers and value lines "
"to terminal width, and the 80-char pre-truncation of bash commands in "
"`format_tool_description` has been removed. Long commands and file paths "
"display fully."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:217
msgid "Auto-Fallback on Rate Limits (v0.2.98)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:219
msgid ""
"When the primary provider hits a rate or account limit mid-stream, OpenCrabs "
"catches the `RateLimitExceeded` error, saves the current conversation state, "
"and **resumes the same conversation on a fallback provider** configured in "
"`[providers.fallback]`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:221
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[providers.fallback]\n"
"enabled = true\n"
"providers = [\"openrouter\", \"anthropic\"]  # tried in order\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:227
msgid ""
"The fallback chain reads from config at startup. `has_fallback_provider()` "
"and `try_get_fallback_provider()` are available at runtime for dynamic "
"queries."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:229
msgid "Two-Tier Context Budget Enforcement"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:231
msgid ""
"Compaction budget scales proportionally to `max_tokens` instead of a "
"hardcoded 170k, supporting custom providers with different context windows:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:233
msgid "**65% soft trigger**: LLM compaction with retries (preserves meaning)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:234
msgid "**90% hard floor**: Forced truncation to 75% (cannot fail)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:235
msgid "Pre-truncate target: 85% of max_tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:236
msgid ""
"Compaction is **silent to user**: summary written to memory log only, no "
"chat spam"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:238
msgid "Mid-Stream Decode Retry (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:240
msgid ""
"Transient stream decoding errors now trigger a **3x backoff retry** before "
"falling back to the provider fallback chain. This reduces false provider "
"switches caused by momentary network glitches."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:242
msgid "SIGINT Handler + Panic Hook (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:244
msgid ""
"Proper terminal restoration on crash or Ctrl+C via custom SIGINT handler and "
"panic hook. No more garbled terminal after interrupt, the handler restores "
"raw mode, cursor visibility, and alternate screen before exiting."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:246
msgid "Proactive Rate Limiting (v0.2.99)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:248
msgid ""
"For OpenRouter `:free` models, OpenCrabs paces requests automatically using "
"a shared global static limiter to avoid account-level bans. The rate "
"limiter's first-call sentinel (`last_granted=0`) no longer causes an "
"unnecessary sleep."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:250
msgid "RSI Alert Suppression (v0.3.13)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:252
msgid ""
"RSI alerts are now suppressed when the feedback dimension already has a fix "
"commit in the recent git history. This prevents the agent from alerting on "
"issues that have already been addressed. Stale alerts also age out via a "
"sliding window on tool failure stats."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:254
msgid "Expanded Phantom Detection (v0.3.17)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:256
msgid "The phantom detector now catches additional patterns:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:257
msgid ""
"**\"Now \\<file-op gerund>\" phantoms**: catches phrases like \"Now "
"creating...\", \"Now writing...\", \"Now editing...\" where the model "
"narrates a file operation without actually executing it"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:258
msgid ""
"**Build/deploy intent + past-tense completion claims**, catches when the "
"model claims to have built or deployed something without running the actual "
"commands"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:259
msgid ""
"**Module extraction**: gaslighting and phantom detectors extracted into "
"their own dedicated module for cleaner maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:261 src/features/self-improvement.md:153
msgid "RSI Escalation for Repeat Violations (v0.3.17)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:263
msgid ""
"RSI now bumps a violation counter on existing rules instead of deduping "
"repeat violations away. Rules that keep getting broken get louder, not "
"silenced. This prevents the agent from ignoring persistent failure patterns."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:265
msgid "Partial JSON Repair (v0.3.17)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:267
msgid "A new `json_repair` module automatically fixes common JSON corruption:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:268
msgid "Closes unterminated strings"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:269
msgid "Balances brackets"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:270
msgid "Strips trailing commas"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:271
msgid "Drops trailing keys-without-value"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:273
msgid ""
"Wired into 5 drop sites across OpenAI-compatible providers and the "
"ContentBlockStop finalizer. Unrecoverable input returns a `{\"_partial\": "
"..., \"_repair_failed\": true}` envelope instead of crashing the turn."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:275
msgid "Upstream Template Sync (v0.3.15)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:277
msgid ""
"Brain file templates are now automatically synced from the upstream "
"OpenCrabs repo. The sync uses version gating (only applies templates from "
"newer versions) and append-only diffs (never overwrites existing content). "
"This ensures you always get the latest brain file improvements without "
"losing your customizations."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:279
msgid "Browser Resilience (v0.3.18)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:281
msgid "Multiple browser reliability improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:282
msgid ""
"**Network idle wait after navigate**: now waits for `networkIdle` instead of "
"just CDP `load` event, catching async fetches"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:283
msgid ""
"**CDP manager lock released before await**: lock was held during screenshot "
"await, blocking concurrent browser operations"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:284
msgid ""
"**CDP pre-flight health check**: added health check before screenshot "
"capture to prevent stale connection failures"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:285
msgid ""
"**Browser navigate errors logged**: navigate errors no longer silently "
"swallowed with `let _ =`, now logged at WARN"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:287
msgid "Cloud Handshake Timeout (v0.3.18)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:289
msgid ""
"Bumped cloud provider handshake timeout from 30s to 60s. Routing proxies "
"like dialagram legitimately take 20-45s; 30s was killing mid-request on "
"slow-but-healthy providers."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:291
msgid "Gemini API Key Security Fix (v0.3.18)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:293
msgid ""
"Fixed CodeQL #64 (HIGH): Gemini API key was leaked in URL query string "
"(`?key=...`) in `analyze_video`'s resumable upload init and file-state "
"polling. Moved to `x-goog-api-key` header, matching `analyze_image` and "
"`generate_image`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:295
msgid "Stream & TUI Fixes (v0.3.18)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:297
msgid ""
"**File paths starting with `/` no longer treated as slash command typos**, "
"`/Users/.../file.pdf yo crabs check this` triggered \"Unknown command\". "
"Added `looks_like_file_path()` helper gating both TUI and channel handlers."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:298
msgid ""
"**Truncation continuations no longer trigger provider fallback**, "
"mid-sentence continuations should stay on the same provider. Fallback now "
"skipped for truncation paths."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:299
msgid ""
"**Fallback error reason surfaced in TUI**: when fallback fired, the "
"underlying error was swallowed. Now shows as a system message."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:300
msgid ""
"**Pipe-delimited rows hard-broken**: when not recognized as a table, pipe "
"rows ran together. Added hard-break between rows."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:302
msgid "v0.3.25 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:304
msgid ""
"**Compaction dropped 55% kept-tail**: summary IS the conversation now, no "
"more redundant tail retention"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:305
msgid ""
"**Self-heal 5-nudge budget**: reasoning-only turns get 5 nudges before "
"sticky fallback, preventing empty replies from silently dropping"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:306
msgid ""
"**Completion-escape clause**: phantom enforcement messages now have escape "
"clause to prevent infinite loops"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:307
msgid ""
"**Scroll fixes**: removed `load_more_history()` from scroll handler "
"(overshoot fix), preserved scroll during streaming, skip first-render "
"compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:308
msgid ""
"**Brain file cleanup_intent**: `write_opencrabs_file` now accepts "
"`cleanup_intent` flag for user-driven maintenance. RSI agent blocked from "
"shrinking brain files (issue #103)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:309
msgid ""
"**Channel improvements**: WhatsApp photo batching for multi-image uploads, "
"Telegram `media_group_id`\\-based batching, Gemini schema strips "
"`default`/`example` from tool schemas (#101, @leshchenko1979)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:310
msgid ""
"**Custom provider model selection persistence**, properly saves and displays "
"custom provider model selection"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:311
msgid ""
"**Compaction prompt dominance fix**: plan tool descriptions and scroll "
"sensitivity improvements"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:313
msgid "v0.3.23 Fixes (Hotfix Release)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:315
msgid ""
"**Phantom detection restored**: v0.3.21's turn-level "
"`tools_executed_this_turn` gate was too aggressive: once any tool ran in a "
"turn, phantom detection went silent for the rest of the turn, letting "
"fabricated wrap-up text reach the TUI. Dropped the gate from all three "
"phantom branches."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:316
msgid ""
"**Self-heal never aborts**: stuck-intent-loop now fast-escalates to sticky "
"fallback instead of aborting; cap-exhaustion resets retry counter and "
"injects hard nudge; `phantom_retries_used` now tracks consecutive phantoms "
"since last real tool. Recovery always retries or falls back."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:317
msgid ""
"**Brain file guardrail**: generic `write_file` / `edit_file` now refuse to "
"modify protected brain files (SOUL.md, USER.md, TOOLS.md, etc.), preventing "
"accidental clobber. Routed through `write_opencrabs_file` instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:318
msgid ""
"**A2A approval policy wired**: A2A `message/send` tasks now resolve approval "
"policy via `check_approval_policy()`. With `auto-always` set, tools "
"auto-approve; otherwise returns warning. Fixes \"Tool requires approval but "
"no approval mechanism configured\" errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:319
msgid ""
"**Channel `/new` session switching fixed**: `/new` now uses per-message "
"resolver's title format everywhere (Telegram, Discord, Slack), so session "
"switching works across all channels."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:320
msgid ""
"**Version-aware model sort**: when OpenAI-compatible servers return zero or "
"identical `created` timestamps, extracts numeric segments from model names "
"and sorts newest version first. Fixes meaningless model lists on "
"vLLM/llama.cpp."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:322
msgid "v0.3.22 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:324
msgid ""
"**Compaction typing without banner**: reverted the visible \"🗜️ Compacting "
"context\" banner text. Now uses typing-only refresh (Telegram "
"`send_chat_action(Typing)`, Discord `broadcast_typing` loop) keeping the "
"\"is typing\" indicator alive during the 10-60s compaction window silently."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:325
msgid ""
"**Channel `/new` archive consistency**: unified archive behavior across all "
"channels: non-owner sessions get archived (so next title lookup resolves "
"cleanly), owner sessions stay non-archived and remain visible in `/sessions`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:327
msgid "v0.3.21 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:329
msgid ""
"**Multi-language phantom detection via compile-time TOML**, replaced regex "
"patterns per language with TOML-defined char sets compiled into build-time "
"match arms. New languages added by editing TOML, no Rust changes. "
"Cross-language regression test added."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:330
msgid ""
"**Self-heal pipeline hardened**: phantom detection gated on turn-level tool "
"execution, phantom iterations no longer persisted to DB, phantom text "
"stripped from context before next turn, sticky fallback applied on exhaust."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:331
msgid ""
"**OpenAI-compatible image generation**: new image generation backend calling "
"any `/v1/images/generations` endpoint. Providers override generation model "
"independently via `generation_model` config field."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:332
msgid ""
"**Working directory visible across tools**: working directory now visible to "
"all tools within the same iteration."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:333
msgid ""
"**Compaction banner stripped from context**: compaction banner text no "
"longer fed to LLM context, preventing models from echoing it back."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:334
msgid ""
"**Pipe-separate model callback**: custom-provider model callbacks now "
"pipe-separated so colons in provider names (e.g. \"Qwen: DashScope\") "
"survive parse."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:335
msgid ""
"**Custom-provider model selection persists**: `/models` dialog now correctly "
"saves and syncs live model list for custom providers."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:336
msgid ""
"**`one_shot_pct` display corrected**: fixed incorrect percentage display in "
"usage dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:337
msgid ""
"**Session `updated_at` touched on switch**: session last-modified timestamp "
"updated when switching sessions via Telegram, preventing stale session "
"resolution."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:339
msgid "v0.3.19 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:341
msgid ""
"**Cron provider/model cross-contamination fixed**, cron's `execute_job` "
"called global `swap_provider()` instead of session-scoped "
"`swap_provider_for_session()`, so concurrent cron jobs on the shared `Cron` "
"session overwrote each other's provider. Now each job swaps on its own "
"session ID."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:342
msgid ""
"**Cron mismatched pair validation**: reversed cron config (e.g. "
"`default_model = \"zhipu\"` where `zhipu` is a provider name) produced "
"impossible pairs like `dialagram/zhipu` that timed out with no diagnostics. "
"Added validation: if `effective_model` is not in the provider's "
"`supported_models()`, the job is skipped with a loud error."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:343
msgid ""
"**Windows CI test failures fixed**: `tool_loop_helpers_test.rs` used "
"hardcoded Unix `/tmp/` paths and `/etc/hosts` assertions. Added "
"platform-specific test variants with `#[cfg(unix)]` / `#[cfg(windows)]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:344
msgid ""
"**CI Node 24 forced upgrade removed**: removed "
"`FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24: true` env var that broke "
"`actions/cache@v4` with `punycode` deprecation on Node 21+."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:345
msgid ""
"**Codex OAuth device flow field names fixed**: OpenAI's device auth API uses "
"non-standard field names (`device_auth_id` instead of `device_code`, string "
"`interval` instead of number, `expires_at` instead of `expires_in`). Fixed "
"with serde aliases and custom deserializer."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:346
msgid ""
"**Codex OAuth verification URL corrected**: was hardcoded to non-existent "
"`auth.openai.com/verify`, changed to `auth.openai.com/codex/device` matching "
"Codex CLI."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:347
msgid ""
"**Codex OAuth model list curated**: `/models` dialog showed non-OpenAI "
"models (Phi-4, Llama, Mistral) because the `codex` provider ID wasn't mapped "
"to the curated GPT-5 model list."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:349
msgid "v0.3.26 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:351
msgid ""
"**Hashline collision detection** (#105): pure content hash prevents "
"line-shift avalanche when lines are inserted/deleted above a hash anchor. On "
"collision, escalates to `edit_file` fallback instead of corrupting the edit"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:352
msgid ""
"**RSI brain file hygiene** (#111): rejects raw failure-event logs from being "
"written to brain files. RSI now sanitizes feedback dimensions before "
"persisting"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:353
msgid ""
"**Tool error output** (#113): tool errors now include stdout/stderr in error "
"content, ANSI escape sequences stripped, 8000 char cap to prevent context "
"blowout"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:355
msgid "v0.3.27 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:357
msgid ""
"**Ctx budget baseline on channel `/new`**: shows calibrated baseline "
"immediately after `/new` instead of waiting for first message"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:358
msgid ""
"**Auto-title session fix** (#114): preserves `[chat:ID]` suffix to prevent "
"title duplication on subsequent auto-title fires"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:359
msgid ""
"**Sessions display** (#115): arrow prefix + \"current\" label instead of "
"checkmark for clearer session switching UI"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:361
msgid "v0.3.28 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:363
msgid ""
"**Voicebox + STT/TTS fallback chains**: 2s liveness probe detects dead audio "
"devices, librosa error translator surfaces actionable messages instead of "
"Python tracebacks, per-provider fallback chains configured in `config.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:364
msgid ""
"**Browser multi-step navigation hardening** (6 commits): `text=`/`xpath=` "
"selector prefixes, recovery hints on click failures, semantic loop detection "
"(4+ screenshots in 8 iterations triggers abort), no-op screenshot rejection, "
"same-URL short-circuit"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:365
msgid ""
"**Tool-call shape recovery**: dict-by-call-id extraction for "
"Qwen-3.7-max-preview regression where tool calls arrive as flat dicts "
"instead of nested arrays"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:366
msgid ""
"**Edit tool improvements** (#117): fuzzy line-sequence fallback when exact "
"match fails, hashline docs clarification"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:367
msgid ""
"**Brain backup rotation**: max 5 backups per file, max 7 days old, "
"preventing unbounded `.bak` accumulation"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:368
msgid ""
"**Auto-title fixes** (#118, #120): fires on FIRST turn (not second), retries "
"on LLM failure instead of giving up"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:369
msgid ""
"**Ctx counter real-time only** (#119): ripped out calibration system "
"entirely, uses provider-reported `input_tokens` verbatim. No more \"0/max\" "
"for uncalibrated providers"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:370
msgid ""
"**Profile brain-template seeding**: seeds 8 templates on `profile create`, "
"recovery path for empty profiles"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:372
msgid "v0.3.29 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:374
msgid ""
"**Auto-title thinking-block fallback** (#121): reasoning models returning "
"only a Thinking block (no Text block) now get a title extracted from the "
"thinking content instead of dropping silently. `extract_title_candidate` "
"falls back to `pluck_title_from_thinking` (last quoted phrase, then last "
"short sentence)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:375
msgid ""
"**Telegram label-drift fix** (PR #123 @leshchenko1979): auto-titled sessions "
"no longer overwritten on every subsequent message. `should_refresh_label` "
"policy only refreshes default→default-different or group label changes, "
"never auto-titled or custom titles. Chat→session binding on `/sessions` "
"switch"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:377
msgid "v0.3.30 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:379
msgid ""
"**5-language deferment stall detection**: self-heal catches \"I need to X\" "
"/ \"I have to X\" / \"I must X\" / \"I should X\" patterns in English, "
"Spanish, Portuguese, French, and Russian"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:380
msgid ""
"**Follow-up message = ESC x2 cancel**: all four channel handlers treat a "
"follow-up message during an active agent run as double-Escape cancel, then "
"starts fresh"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:381
msgid ""
"**Dynamic Telegram status messages**: replaced hardcoded quips with "
"context-aware messages showing actual tool being called, tokens streamed, "
"and elapsed time"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:382
msgid ""
"**rename_session rejects empty titles** (#128): whitespace-only titles "
"rejected so sessions can't become unidentifiable"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:384
msgid "v0.3.31 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:386
msgid ""
"**Fun POST-COMPACTION PROTOCOL prompts**: after compaction, the agent "
"receives a playful system prompt instead of a sterile summary marker. These "
"rotating prompts (e.g. \"You just woke up from a nap. The summary above is "
"everything you remember.\") make the post-compaction experience less "
"robotic. Users can opt out with `[agent] silent_compaction = true` in "
"config.toml."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:387
msgid ""
"**Telegram forum topic routing**: in supergroups with topics enabled, "
"`thread_id` is tracked through the full pipeline. The agent can use "
"`list_topics` to map topic names to IDs, then route responses to specific "
"topics via `thread_id` on send/reply/send_photo."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:388
msgid ""
"**PDF `page_range` param**: `parse_document` now accepts `page_range` "
"strings like `\"1-30\"`, `\"5,7,10-15\"`, or `\"3\"` for targeted "
"extraction. Text-first routing skips Gemini for text-native PDFs. Inline "
"preview cap raised to ~60 pages."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:390
msgid "v0.3.32 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:392
msgid ""
"**Evolve hardening** (#136): the `/evolve` command now handles busy Linux "
"binaries with a remove+rename dance (can't overwrite a running binary on "
"Linux), delayed `systemd-run` restart to let the current process finish "
"cleanly, structured tracing for better error diagnosis, and a pre-flight "
"`count_matching_systemd_units` check to avoid restarting when multiple "
"OpenCrabs instances are running."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:394
msgid "v0.3.33 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:396
msgid ""
"**User-correction metadata** (#138, PR #140): `display_text_override` now "
"captures the actual user message text instead of the 236-character Telegram "
"channel prefix that was previously stored. This makes user correction "
"entries in the feedback ledger readable and actionable."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:398
msgid "v0.3.34 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:400
msgid ""
"**`follow_up_question` race fix (closes #142)**: all four channels "
"(Telegram, Discord, Slack, WhatsApp) now flush intermediate text handles "
"before presenting the follow-up keyboard. Prevents the race where the bot's "
"in-progress message got orphaned or duplicated when the user tapped a button "
"mid-stream. Each channel got its own atomic commit with per-channel "
"regression tests pinning the flush-before-keyboard sequence."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:401
msgid ""
"**`follow_up_question` display polish (closes #148)**: Telegram keyboard is "
"now single-column with a 40-character label cap (rejects options longer than "
"40 chars in the tool validator with a clear error). Rolling \"Running "
"follow_up_question (16s)\" status is suppressed while the keyboard is "
"pending, and the LLM is now instructed to call the tool silently without "
"echoing the question text in surrounding prose. Discord left alone due to "
"its 5-ActionRow-per-message hard limit."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:402
msgid ""
"**Phantom detector hardening**: two narration shapes had been leaking past "
"the phantom detector: pronounless deferment (`Need to read the X`) and bare "
"gerunds (`Reading the current state of the affected files`). Added 28 "
"pronounless EN variants, 15 telegraphic FR `besoin de` variants, and "
"gerund+determiner bigrams. New regression file pins both leaked sentences "
"verbatim. Follow-up fixed French accent detection: `detect_language` missed "
"`é/è/ë/ü`, so French narration fell through to English and the new `besoin "
"de` phrases never matched. Added the 4 markers."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:403
msgid ""
"**Fallback provider cascade (closes #152)**: `/models` swaps and session "
"restores were storing a raw provider instead of wrapping it in "
"`FallbackProvider`, so the fallback cascade could not fire on 5xx/429 errors "
"after a model switch. Every active provider now gets wrapped unless it is "
"already a chain or no fallbacks are configured. 174-line integration test "
"simulating 5xx cascades across swapped providers."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:404
msgid ""
"**Error persistence**: agent failures now persist as permanent chat bubbles "
"with actionable wording on TUI and channels instead of vanishing after the "
"turn. UTF-8 panic after redact-prefix scan fixed by snapping to char "
"boundary."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:405
msgid ""
"**FINISHING A TURN rewrite**: split the brain preamble directive into "
"side-effect vs analysis response shapes, added a nudge on empty data-fetch "
"closes so the agent never ends a turn silently after running research tools, "
"and requires an explicit acknowledgement sentence instead of letting "
"`finish_reason: stop` with no content reach the user."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:406
msgid ""
"**Claude CLI model auto-learn**: footer showed Opus 4.7 after Anthropic "
"shipped 4.8 because `default_for_alias` hardcoded `opus -> opus-4-7`. Now "
"the provider learns the CLI-resolved version from `message_start` events, "
"persists to `~/.opencrabs/claude_cli_models.json` (rewriting only when the "
"value changes), and the TUI refreshes the session model live so the footer "
"self-corrects to the actual version without code changes. "
"`default_for_alias` prefers the learned cache and falls back to a build-time "
"seed only on a fresh install."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:407
msgid ""
"**tok/s in channel footers**: channel context budget footers showed only "
"`ctx: XK/YK Z%` while the TUI also showed `| N tok/s`. Added "
"`tokens_per_second: Option<f64>` to `AgentResponse`, extended "
"`format_ctx_footer` to accept a third `tps` parameter, computed tok/s from "
"`total_output_tokens / turn_duration` across the whole turn in "
"`tool_loop.rs`, and wired it through all four channels."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:409
msgid "Unreleased (post-v0.3.33)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:411
msgid ""
"**Phantom post-success exemption**: the phantom detector used to fire on "
"short completion acknowledgments like \"Pushed.\", \"Done.\", or \"Committed "
"as abc123\" because those look like past-tense completion claims without a "
"tool call. But when the agent just finished a real tool run, that one-line "
"ack is the _correct_ behavior. A turn-scoped "
"`tool_calls_completed_this_turn` counter and a `phantom_eligible` gate now "
"suppress phantom detection once real tool calls have landed in the current "
"turn. The complementary `FINISHING A TURN` brain preamble directive tells "
"the agent to reply with one short ack, skip verification re-runs, and stop "
"restating conclusions in different wording."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:412
msgid ""
"**`follow_up_question` intermediate flush** (issue #142): when the agent "
"called `follow_up_question` after typing an explanatory preamble, "
"Telegram/Discord/Slack/WhatsApp sometimes delivered the button block "
"_before_ the preamble text because intermediate text sat in a 500ms-polled "
"queue while `follow_up_question` sent directly. All four channel handlers "
"now flush pending intermediate `JoinHandle`s before dispatching the "
"question, guaranteeing the explanatory text renders above the buttons."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:414
msgid "v0.3.36 Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:416
msgid ""
"**Near-miss tool name self-heal (closes #176)**: when the model guesses a "
"wrong tool name (e.g. `tg_send_message` instead of `telegram_send`), the "
"tool registry now tries three fallback strategies before returning NotFound: "
"(1) normalized match (strip underscores, lowercase), (2) abbreviation "
"expansion (`tg` → `telegram`, `wa` → `whatsapp`), (3) typo fallback "
"(Levenshtein distance). Conservative: only heals on a unique high-confidence "
"match, so ambiguous guesses still return an error."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:417
msgid ""
"**Retry overhaul**: patient backoff defaults changed from 100ms hammering to "
"1s/2s/4s/8s. Rate limits now retry in-place (3 retries) before falling "
"through the fallback chain. Hard-down endpoints (DNS failure, connection "
"refused) fail fast instead of wasting retries. Transient 4xx HTML infra "
"pages (Cloudflare, nginx error pages) are retried. Each retry surfaces as a "
"`RetryAttempt N/M - reason` event to the user."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:418
msgid ""
"**Provider/model contamination prevention**: atomic provider+model swap "
"across 27 call sites prevents the footer from showing a stale provider after "
"switching panes or sessions."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:419
msgid ""
"**Secret redaction expanded**: query-param keys (`?api_key=...`) and URL "
"passwords (`https://user:pass@host`) now redacted alongside Bearer tokens "
"and API key patterns. RSI TUI notifications also redacted."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:421
msgid "v0.3.35 Phantom Hardening"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:423
msgid ""
"**Re-engaged on forward intent**: phantom detector now re-engages self-heal "
"when forward intent is detected after a successful tool call, preventing the "
"agent from narrating what it's about to do instead of just doing it."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:424
msgid ""
"**Five-language cleanup**: destructive verb intent phrases cleaned up across "
"EN, ES, FR, PT, and RU. Prevents the agent from narrating destructive "
"actions (\"I'll now delete the file\") when it should just execute the tool."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:426
msgid "Thinking-Loop Timeout (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:428
msgid ""
"A new **thinking-loop timeout** catches the agent stuck in an infinite "
"reasoning loop (producing thought tokens but never emitting a tool call or "
"response). When the timeout fires:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:430
msgid "The stuck stream is terminated"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:431
msgid "Phantom enforcement retry fires (nudges the agent to produce real output)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:432
msgid "If still stuck after retries, sticky fallback provider kicks in"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:434
msgid ""
"This eliminates the \"agent appears to be thinking forever but never does "
"anything\" failure mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:436
msgid "Expanded Phantom Detection (v0.3.76–v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:438
