msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:440 src/features/self-improvement.md:247
msgid "v0.3.76 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:441
msgid ""
"**File-delivery claims**: catches \"I've sent the file\" / \"document "
"delivered\" when no file-sending tool ran"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:442
msgid ""
"**Null-effect tool calls**: tools that execute but produce no observable "
"effect no longer grant phantom immunity"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:443
msgid ""
"**Command verification**: quoted commands are checked against what the turn "
"actually ran"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:444
msgid ""
"**Evidence checking**: quoted evidence (output, logs) is verified against "
"actual tool returns"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:445
msgid ""
"**Investigation claims**: \"I investigated\" / \"I looked into\" counts as a "
"completion claim requiring evidence"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:446
msgid ""
"**Both-ends check**: examines both the lead-in AND the wrap-up of a turn, "
"not just the opening"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:447
msgid ""
"**Self-update claims**: \"I updated my memory\" / \"I noted this\" counts as "
"a completion claim"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:449 src/features/self-improvement.md:252
msgid "v0.3.78 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:450
msgid ""
"**Shipped-and-tracked claims**: \"shipped and tracked in issue #N\" without "
"actual gh/git calls"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:451
msgid ""
"**Colloquial delivery claims**: \"that's out the door\", \"it's in your "
"inbox\", casual completion language"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:452
msgid ""
"**Media-delivery claims**: \"I've attached the image\" / \"video sent\" "
"without media tools running"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:454
msgid "v0.3.75 Hardening"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:456
msgid ""
"**Bounded self-heal loop**: the phantom self-heal loop is now bounded "
"instead of re-nudging forever, and discarded phantom self-heal narration is "
"stripped from the live buffer so it never reaches the chat."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:457
msgid ""
"**Patient mid-stream retry**: mid-stream retry is more patient: 5 attempts "
"with exponential backoff instead of giving up early."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:458
msgid ""
"**Flaky 404 retried**: a flaky-provider 404 is retried instead of being "
"treated as a permanent failure."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:459
msgid ""
"**Multilingual hallucination detection**: image-generation hallucination "
"detection (a media claim with no marker and zero tool calls) now works "
"across languages, and self-heal no longer delivers an image hallucination "
"when it gives up."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:460
msgid ""
"**Poisoned-session recovery**: auto-recovers from a repetitive-tool-call "
"poisoned session instead of looping on the same broken call."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:461
msgid ""
"**Phantom verdict on recovery paths**: the turn-end phantom verdict now "
"catches narration delivered via recovery paths, and issue-tracker actions "
"count as completion claims."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:463
msgid "Loop Guards (v0.3.80)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:465
msgid "Three guards stop the agent repeating itself (#957, #961):"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:467
msgid ""
"**Cross-turn announcement loop guard**: detects when the agent keeps "
"announcing the same action across turns without actually doing it"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:468
msgid ""
"**Near-match loop guard**: catches reworded repetitions of the same tool "
"call, generalized to ALL tools, not just bash"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:469
msgid ""
"**Mid-turn announcement checks**: reworded announcement loops are caught "
"inside the turn, not only between turns"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-healing.md:471
msgid ""
"When the loop detector kills a stalled turn, that kill **reaches the "
"fallback chain** (#1023): it is raised as a provider-attributable error so "
"the turn can retry with another provider instead of surfacing as a hard "
"failure, and it is no longer misreported as a provider fault. Spent "
"thinking-loop budget is routed into the fallback chain the same way (#1021)."
msgstr ""

