#: src/features/self-improvement.md:97
msgid "Repeat-Violation Escalation"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:99
msgid ""
"RSI tracks violation counters inline in brain file rules. When a rule keeps "
"getting broken, RSI bumps the counter and appends evidence (dates, session "
"IDs). Rules that keep getting broken get louder, not silenced. This is the "
"escalation pattern that makes RSI effective at fixing persistent bad habits."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:101
msgid "RSI Proposals"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:103
msgid ""
"The RSI loop can propose new dynamic tools and slash commands based on gaps "
"it observes in the agent's capabilities. Proposals land in TOML inboxes at:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:117
msgid "How Proposals Work"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:119
msgid ""
"RSI analyzes feedback and notices the agent repeatedly working around a "
"missing capability"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:120
msgid ""
"RSI drafts a tool or command definition with a rationale citing the evidence"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:121
msgid ""
"Proposal lands in the inbox: reviewed via Mission Control or the "
"`rsi_proposals` tool"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:122
msgid ""
"User applies or rejects: applied entries go to `tools.toml`/`commands.toml`, "
"rejected entries are archived with an optional reason"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:124
msgid "When RSI Proposes a Tool"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:126
msgid ""
"A specific bash command appears repeatedly across sessions (e.g. `gh issue "
"list`, `docker ps`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:127
msgid ""
"The agent calls `http_request` to the same endpoint multiple times with "
"similar payloads"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:128
msgid ""
"Only safe-by-default tools are proposed (read-only verbs, GET requests). "
"Shell-based tools always set `requires_approval=true`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:130
msgid "When RSI Proposes a Command"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:132
msgid "The user types `/something` repeatedly that doesn't exist"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:133
msgid ""
"A common multi-step prompt gets reused verbatim, a slash command saves typing"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:135
msgid "Safety Guardrails"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:137
msgid ""
"**RSI never installs directly**: proposals require user approval via Mission "
"Control or the `rsi_proposals` tool"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:138
msgid ""
"**No destructive proposals**: RSI will never propose `rm`, `dd`, `mv`, or "
"any shell tool with destructive side effects"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:139
msgid ""
"**Deduplication**: if a proposal was already filed and not applied, RSI "
"won't repropose it"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:140
msgid "**One proposal per cycle**: quality over quantity"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:141
msgid ""
"**Evidence required**: every proposal cites the feedback events that drove it"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:143
msgid "RSI Hardening (v0.3.13)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:145
msgid ""
"**Append-only brain files**: brain files (SOUL.md, TOOLS.md, etc.) are now "
"append-only with backup-before-write. The agent can only add new content, "
"never delete or overwrite existing lines. This prevents accidental data loss "
"from bad self-improvements."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:146
msgid ""
"**Upstream template sync**: brain file templates are automatically synced "
"from the upstream repo with version gating and append-only diffs. You get "
"the latest improvements without losing your customizations."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:147
msgid ""
"**RSI alert suppression**: alerts are suppressed when the dimension already "
"has a fix commit, preventing noise on already-addressed issues."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:149
msgid "RSI Autonomous Proposals (v0.3.16)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:151
msgid ""
"The RSI loop can now propose new tools and slash commands autonomously. "
"Proposals land in the Mission Control inbox for review, the agent identifies "
"gaps from feedback data and drafts solutions, but installation requires "
"human approval via the inbox UI or `/mission-control`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:155
msgid ""
"RSI now bumps a violation counter on existing rules instead of deduping "
"repeat violations away. When a rule keeps getting broken across multiple "
"sessions, the escalation counter increases and the agent prioritizes fixing "
"that pattern. This prevents persistent bad habits from being silently "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:157
msgid "v0.3.10 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:159
msgid ""
"**Cycle summaries no longer truncated**: full text displays in TUI instead "
"of cutting off mid-sentence"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:160
msgid ""
"**Phantom detection reduced to 2-signal requirement**, needs both intent "
"keyphrase AND zero tool calls before flagging, eliminating spurious "
"self-heal triggers"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:161
msgid ""
"**Uses active provider**: respects current provider/model config instead of "
"hardcoded Anthropic"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:162
msgid ""
"**Persistent session reuse**: one session per cycle, survives app restarts "
"by persisting `last_cycle` timestamp"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:163
msgid ""
"**Skips unchanged feedback**: if feedback count hasn't changed, skips "
"analysis to avoid wasted LLM calls"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:165
msgid "v0.3.11 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:167
msgid ""
"**DashScope migration**: Qwen OAuth rotation replaced with simple API-key "
"provider, deleting ~2,500 lines of complexity"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:168
msgid ""
"**Local model tool-call extraction**: auto-extracts tool calls from text "
"content: bare JSON `{\"tool_calls\":[...]}`, Claude-style XML "
"`<TOOLNAME><PARAM>value</PARAM></TOOLNAME>`, and Qwen-specific `<!-- "
"tool_calls -->` markers"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:169
msgid ""
"**40+ TUI/self-heal fixes**: narrowed phantom gate, split thinking per "
"iteration, anti-code-block nudge for local models, tighter phantom scope, "
"mid-turn \"Let me see:\" catch, backtick code reference detection"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:170
msgid ""
"**Per-session provider isolation**: each session carries its own provider "
"instance; no global swap affecting all sessions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:171
msgid ""
"**Sub-agent `AwaitingInput` state**: `wait_agent` polls state and returns "
"partial progress on timeout instead of deadlocking"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:173
msgid "v0.3.20 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:175
msgid ""
"**RSI home directory resolution fixed**: RSI now resolves `~` to the actual "
"home directory instead of using CWD-relative paths, preventing brain file "
"writes to wrong locations"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:176
msgid ""
"**Bare tool-call arrays caught**: top-level arrays from models no longer "
"crash RSI's feedback dimension parsing; wrapped correctly before recording"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:178
msgid "v0.3.21 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:180
msgid ""
"**Multi-language phantom detection**: compile-time TOML char sets replaced "
"language-specific regex patterns. RSI feedback now works with all supported "
"languages via the new char-set system. Cross-language regression test added."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:181
msgid ""
"**RSI cycle output dedup by hashing**: cycle output dedup now uses hash "
"comparison of assembled opportunities instead of string matching, preventing "
"duplicate cycle reports."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:182
msgid ""
"**Sticky fallback on phantom exhaust**: when phantom detection exhausts "
"retries, RSI applies sticky fallback provider to prevent cascading failures."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:183
msgid ""
"**Phantom iterations not persisted**: phantom iterations no longer written "
"to DB, keeping history clean of failed self-heal attempts."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:184
msgid ""
"**OpenAI-compatible image generation**: image generation via any "
"`/v1/images/generations` endpoint with configurable `generation_model` "
"override."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:186
msgid "v0.3.23 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:188
msgid ""
"**Brain file clobber guardrail**: generic `write_file` / `edit_file` now "
"refuse protected brain files, routing through `write_opencrabs_file` which "
"enforces append-only, dedup-aware shrink, and `.bak` snapshots."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:189
msgid ""
"**A2A approval policy**: A2A tasks now resolve approval policy correctly. "
"`auto-always` and `auto-session` policies work for remote agents."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:191
msgid "v0.3.25 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:193
msgid ""
"**Brain file cleanup_intent**: `write_opencrabs_file` accepts "
"`cleanup_intent` flag for user-driven brain file maintenance. RSI agent "
"explicitly blocked from shrinking brain files, preventing autonomous "
"self-improvement from accidentally wiping content (issue #103)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:194
msgid ""
"**RTK Token Savings integration**: bundled RTK binary (4MB, v0.40.0) as "
"default feature with zero-config. Works as direct proxy: agent runs `git "
"status`, RTK intercepts output through Rust, filters it, returns "
"token-optimized version. 100+ commands supported (git, cargo, npm, pnpm, "
"docker, kubectl, grep, find, ls, tree, curl), blocklist for interactive/REPL "
"commands (vim, ssh, python, mysql). Binary discovery checks bundled location "
"first, falls back to PATH. `/rtk` slash command shows savings stats. "
"Real-world results: 53.5% token savings across 180 commands (PR #102)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:196
msgid "v0.3.19 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:198
msgid ""
"**RSI feedback records actual model used**: when helpers remap a mismatched "
"model to the provider default, RSI now records the resolved model instead of "
"the impossible original pair. All 3 recording sites in `tool_loop.rs` now "
"resolve the actual model before constructing the feedback dimension"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:199
msgid ""
"**Tool loop reasoning markers persisted**: reasoning content persisted in "
"non-CLI content column so thinking state survives across tool loop iterations"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:200
msgid ""
"**@ file picker fixed for large repos**: recursive walk now skips "
"`.git`/`.hg`/`.svn` directories and raised result cap from 5k to 20k, "
"preventing pack/ref files from exhausting the cap"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:202
msgid "v0.3.26 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:204
msgid ""
"**RSI brain file hygiene**: rejects raw failure-event logs from being "
"written to brain files. Feedback dimensions are sanitized before persisting, "
"preventing noise accumulation in SOUL.md and TOOLS.md"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:205
msgid ""
"**Hashline collision escalation**: when hashline_edit detects a collision "
"(two lines with identical content hashes), RSI escalates to `edit_file` "
"fallback instead of applying a corrupted edit"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:206
msgid ""
"**Dynamic help screen**: help screen auto-generates from `SLASH_COMMANDS` "
"constant, so new commands appear automatically without manual help text "
"updates"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:208
msgid "v0.3.28 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:210
msgid ""
"**Brain backup rotation**: max 5 backups per file, max 7 days old. Prevents "
"unbounded `.bak` accumulation in `~/.opencrabs/` from repeated RSI writes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:211
msgid ""
"**Profile brain-template seeding**: `profile create` now seeds 8 brain file "
"templates automatically, with recovery path for empty profiles. Ensures new "
"profiles start with complete brain file sets"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:212
msgid ""
"**Auto-title retry on LLM failure**: auto-title no longer gives up on first "
"LLM error; retries with backoff before falling back to truncated first "
"message"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:214
msgid "v0.3.30 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:216
msgid ""
"**RSI rejects trivial content**: `self_improve` apply action now rejects "
"trivial test content before it can pollute brain files, preventing noise "
"from accumulating in SOUL.md and TOOLS.md"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:218
msgid "v0.3.31 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:220
msgid ""
"**RSI skill proposals**: `skill` is now a third proposal kind alongside "
"`tool` and `command`. When RSI identifies a multi-stage workflow pattern "
"that recurs across sessions, it proposes a `SKILL.md` file instead of a "
"simple tool or command. Applied skill proposals write to "
"`~/.opencrabs/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and become immediately invocable as "
"`/<name>` across all channels."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:221
msgid ""
"**Bash command visibility**: RSI now sees the actual bash command text plus "
"a subsystem classifier (git, cargo, docker, npm, etc.) in feedback events. "
"This lets RSI identify recurring shell patterns more accurately and propose "
"targeted tools or skills."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:222
msgid ""
"**Successful patterns surface as proposals**: RSI doesn't only react to "
"failures. When a tool/command/skill pattern works reliably across multiple "
"sessions, RSI surfaces it as a proposal to make the pattern more "
"discoverable or ergonomic."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:224
msgid "v0.3.34 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:226
msgid ""
"**Brain dedup scan (closes #147)**: new RSI proposal kind `BrainDedup` that "
"scans all 11 brain files daily, clusters duplicate lines (minimum 10 chars, "
"skips structural markdown like headings and separators), and files dedup "
"proposals into Mission Control with a soft purple badge. Runs every 24 RSI "
"cycles (about once per day at 1-hour intervals), never auto-applies, human "
"approval required through the existing `rsi_proposals` apply/reject flow. "
"Core scan logic in `dedup_scan.rs` (393 lines), hooked into the RSI cycle "
"with periodicity gating, 14 regression tests covering empty files, "
"short-line filtering, cross-file detection, proposal format, and canonical "
"selection."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:227
msgid ""
"**Skill description injection (closes #151)**: skill descriptions were "
"documented in TOOLS.md as LLM auto-invoking triggers but were never actually "
"injected into the system prompt, so the LLM could not auto-invoke from "
"description alone. Added `push_skills_section()` to `prompt_builder.rs` that "
"loads all skills via `crate::brain::skills::load_all_skills()` and formats "
"each as `- skill_name: description`, appending an `## Available Skills` "
"block to both `build_core_brain()` and `build_system_brain()`. 2 regression "
"tests."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:228
msgid ""
"**RSI decorative counters removed (closes #149, PR #150)**: removed the "
"counter-bumping logic that incremented inline counters in SOUL.md like "
"`phantom_tool_call: 219`. These counters were decorative only, nothing read "
"them, and the real canonical source is the SQLite feedback ledger at "
"`~/.opencrabs/feedback.db`. Counters went stale (ledger showed 302, SOUL.md "
"showed 219) and got wiped by upstream template sync. Replaced with evidence "
"appends (date/session). DB stays the single source of truth. Follow-up "
"commit escaped unescaped double quotes the PR introduced in the prompt "
"string literal and added text regression tests."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:230
msgid "v0.3.35 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:232
msgid ""
"**`cycle_number` persistence**: `cycle_number` now persists to "
"`~/.opencrabs/rsi/cycle_number` across TUI restarts. Previously it reset to "
"0 on every process restart, meaning the brain dedup scan (which fires every "
"24 cycles) would never trigger if the TUI restarted more frequently than 24 "
"hours. Now the cycle counter survives restarts and the daily dedup scan "
"fires as intended."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:234
msgid "v0.3.66 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:236
msgid ""
"**Skill candidates from tool sequences**: RSI detects recurring tool "
"sequences as skill candidates. When the agent repeatedly calls the same "
"sequence of tools (e.g. `read_file` → `edit_file` → `bash` with specific "
"patterns), RSI proposes a skill that encapsulates the workflow."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:237
msgid ""
"**Slash commands from repeated asks**: RSI proposes slash commands from "
"repeated user requests. When users type the same multi-word prompt "
"repeatedly, RSI suggests a `/command` that captures the pattern."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:238
msgid ""
"**RSI staleness indicator**: Mission Control shows a staleness indicator for "
"RSI cycles, plus a provider-creation fallback when the primary provider is "
"unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:240
msgid "v0.3.75 Additions"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:242
msgid ""
"**Brain dedup system**: a new `/dedup` command runs an on-demand cross-file "
"brain dedup scan, backed by a post-write scan that fires after brain writes "
"and a weekly cron safety net that catches cross-file duplication. The "
"scanner ignores fenced code and table rows so it only flags real prose "
"duplication."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:243
msgid ""
"**Inline-keyboard dedup approval**: dedup proposals can be approved straight "
"from a Telegram inline keyboard."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:244
msgid ""
"**Brain-file hints on tool misses**: when a tool call misses or errors "
"(including approval-branch errors), the relevant brain notes surface "
"automatically so the agent can self-correct (#767)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:245
msgid ""
"**Wider TOOLS.md load trigger**, routing, skill, and cron questions now "
"proactively load TOOLS.md."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:249
msgid ""
"**RSI /evolve proposal**: when a new OpenCrabs release is available, RSI "
"surfaces it as an `/evolve` proposal in the Mission Control inbox instead of "
"silently ignoring it. The proposal cites the version delta and links to the "
"release notes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:250
msgid ""
"**Config-example tracking**: RSI tracks config examples so pricing fixes and "
"new provider entries reach users through template sync."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:254
msgid ""
"**TOML brain verification**: a new `brain_verify.toml` defines post-write "
"verification rules. After any brain file write, the system re-reads the file "
"and checks required anchors (H1 title, `**Owns:**` header) are still "
"present. If verification fails, the write is flagged."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:255
msgid ""
"**brain_verify Orient gate**: `self_improve` now routes through the "
"epistemic Orient gate before applying changes. The agent must orient (verify "
"current state) before writing, preventing RSI from applying fixes based on "
"stale beliefs about brain file content."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:256
msgid ""
"**RSI digest totals**: the RSI digest now surfaces raw failure totals "
"alongside surfaced opportunities, giving better visibility into what's "
"actually failing vs what RSI chose to act on."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:257
msgid ""
"**Rule size cap**: brain file rules are now capped in size. A narrow "
"consolidation path allows merging related rules, preventing unbounded growth "
"from repeated RSI appends."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/self-improvement.md:258
msgid ""
"**Contradiction scope fix**: brain_verify contradiction matching is now "
"scoped per-entry instead of whole-file, eliminating false positives where "
"unrelated entries triggered contradiction warnings."
msgstr ""

