#: src/features/skills.md:148
msgid ""
"The RSI engine can propose new skills based on usage patterns it observes in "
"the feedback ledger. For example, if the agent repeatedly performs a "
"multi-step workflow that isn't covered by an existing skill, RSI will draft "
"a skill and file it in the [Mission Control](./mission-control.md) inbox for "
"your review."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/skills.md:150
msgid ""
"This is part of the [RSI Proposals "
"system](./self-improvement.md#rsi-proposals): RSI identifies gaps in the "
"agent's capabilities and drafts solutions, but installation always requires "
"your approval."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/skills.md:152
msgid "Slash Command Resolution (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/skills.md:154
msgid ""
"The `slash_command` tool now correctly resolves **skills** and the "
"`/onboard:<topic>` form. Previously, calling a skill via `slash_command` "
"could fail if the skill name didn't exactly match the internal registry key. "
"The resolver now checks skills, built-in commands, and user commands in "
"priority order, and the `/onboard:voice` / `/onboard:provider` / "
"`/onboard:channels` sub-topic forms route correctly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:3
msgid ""
"The TUI is colored by **semantic roles**, not raw hexes. Every render site "
"resolves a role (`accent`, `text_primary`, `selection_bg`, …) through the "
"active theme, so one switch restyles the whole interface at runtime. A theme "
"is **one file, 43 keys, done**."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:7
msgid "Switching themes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:11
msgid "`/theme`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:11
msgid ""
"Opens the interactive picker: `↑`/`↓` (or `j`/`k`) move the cursor and "
"**preview live**, the whole UI recolors under the arrow keys. `Enter` "
"applies and persists, `Esc` (or `q`) cancels and reverts to whatever was "
"active when the picker opened."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:12
msgid "`/theme list`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:12
msgid ""
"Lists built-in themes and user presets, then re-scans "
"`~/.opencrabs/themes/`. Files that fail validation are listed with a "
"human-readable rejection reason, never silently ignored."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:13
msgid "`/theme set <name>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:13
msgid ""
"Applies a theme immediately and writes it to your config. Lookup is "
"case-insensitive across built-ins and user presets; an unknown name tells "
"you to run `/theme list`."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:14
msgid "`/theme reset`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:14
msgid "Returns to the default (`crab-dark`) and clears the config key."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:16
msgid "To pin a theme without the picker, set it in `config.toml`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:18
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tui]\n"
"theme = \"nord\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:23
msgid ""
"The value is applied at boot before the first frame. An empty or unknown "
"name falls back to `crab-dark`. User theme files are re-scanned on every "
"`/theme` invocation, so editing a preset file hot-loads it without "
"restarting the TUI."
msgstr ""

