#: src/features/themes.md:204
msgid "Validation rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:206
msgid ""
"Validation is loud, never silent. A theme file is rejected, with the reason "
"shown by `/theme list`, when it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:209
msgid "**misses any of the 43 roles**: the error names the missing key;"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:210
msgid ""
"**carries an unknown key**: strict typo guard, there is no partial-schema "
"mode;"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:211
msgid "**uses a malformed value**: only `#RRGGBB` or `RRGGBB`, case-insensitive;"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:212
msgid ""
"**fails the contrast floor** (eight reading-critical (foreground, "
"background) pairs must hit **2.5:1** WCAG contrast: "
"`text_primary`/`text_secondary`/`accent`/`success`/`error`/ `warning` on "
"`ink`, `blue_code` on `surface_code`, and `gray_mid` on `surface_panel`. "
"Deliberately dim tiers (`text_muted`, `text_dim`, …) are excluded) dim is "
"their job;"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:216
msgid ""
"**collides with a built-in name**: user files can never shadow a shipped "
"preset."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:218
msgid ""
"Everything else is free for the runtime: each valid theme gets its "
"**ANSI-256 fallback tier derived automatically**, so terminals without "
"truecolor still render it (nearest index in the 6×6×6 cube, grayscale ramp "
"for neutrals)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:222
msgid "Theme enforcement (v0.5.3)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:224
msgid ""
"Every widget in the TUI now resolves its colours through the theme engine, "
"the last hardcoded ANSI sites are gone, and a suite-level guard fails the "
"build if a new raw ANSI colour site appears (#1634). Themes can also declare "
"an optional **canvas background** (the source background carries through "
"catalog conversion), so a theme can restyle the whole terminal canvas, not "
"just the widgets on it."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:230
msgid "Imported themes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:232
msgid ""
"The 31-theme curated pack was generated by the in-tree converter "
"(`tui::theme_catalog`) from two upstream formats:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:235
msgid ""
"**alacritty-theme TOML** (`[colors.primary]` background/foreground plus the "
"16 ANSI colors): the `alacritty/alacritty-theme` catalog, 176 themes;"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:237
msgid ""
"**opencode theme JSON** (`defs` + `theme` token maps with dark/light "
"variants, hex strings, ANSI integers, `defs` references and `\"none\"`), the "
"`sst/opencode` built-in themes, 33 assets."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:241
msgid ""
"Both convert through a **fixed 43-role mapping** (semantic token first, ANSI "
"color or deterministic bg/fg mix as fallback), and every generated file is "
"pre-certified by the same validator user themes face: a converted file that "
"doesn't validate never ships. Each pack file carries a `# source:` "
"provenance header naming the upstream repo, file, and fetch date; the "
"gallery table shows it. Upstream palettes belong to their authors; the pack "
"imports their colors, not their names' goodwill."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/themes.md:248
msgid ""
"The converter is generation-time tooling: the TUI itself only knows the "
"embedded presets and your drop-in files."
msgstr ""

