#: src/features/rtk.md:1
msgid "RTK: Rust Token Killer"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:3
msgid ""
"RTK is natively bundled into OpenCrabs as a built-in feature. It intercepts "
"bash commands before they run, filters and compresses their output, and "
"returns a token-optimized version to the LLM context. The result: **60-90% "
"token savings** on common development commands, which directly translates to "
"lower API costs and faster responses."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:5
msgid "What It Does"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:7
msgid ""
"When OpenCrabs runs a bash command like `git status` or `cargo build`, RTK:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:9
msgid "**Intercepts** the command before execution"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:10
msgid "**Runs** it through RTK's filtering engine"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:11
msgid "**Compresses** verbose output (removes noise, keeps signal)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:12
msgid "**Returns** the optimized output to the agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:14
msgid "The agent sees the same information, but using a fraction of the tokens."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:16
msgid "Real-World Impact"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:18
msgid "From production usage (13,600+ commands executed):"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:22
msgid "**Total Commands**"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:22
msgid "13,600+"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:23
msgid "**Input Tokens**"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/rtk.md:23
