#: src/features/goal.md:1
msgid "Autonomous Goal Loop (/goal)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:3
msgid ""
"The `/goal` command lets you set a high-level goal and have OpenCrabs work "
"toward it **autonomously**, executing actions, self-evaluating with an LLM "
"judge, and continuing until the goal is satisfied or a turn budget runs out."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:7
msgid "**Set a goal**: `/goal <description of what you want>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:8
msgid ""
"**The agent loops**: executes an action, then an LLM judge evaluates whether "
"the goal is met"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:9
msgid ""
"**Self-correction**: if the goal isn't satisfied, the agent continues with a "
"correction prompt"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:10
msgid ""
"**Completion**: the loop ends when the judge says the goal is met, or the "
"turn budget (default 20 turns) is exhausted"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:12
msgid "This is fully hands-off. Set the goal, walk away, come back to results."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:34
msgid "Turn Budget"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:36
msgid ""
"The default turn budget is **20 autonomous turns**. Each turn is one full "
"LLM round-trip (action + evaluation). The agent uses a lightweight LLM judge "
"to evaluate progress, keeping costs low."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:38
msgid ""
"If the budget runs out before the goal is satisfied, the agent reports what "
"it accomplished and what remains."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:40
msgid "Best Practices"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:42
msgid ""
"**Be specific**: \"Fix the login bug\" works better than \"make the app "
"better\""
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:43
msgid "**Set boundaries**: mention files, modules, or constraints in the goal"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:44
msgid ""
"**Use for multi-step tasks**: `/goal` shines on tasks that need repeated "
"execution and self-correction"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:45
msgid ""
"**Check status**: use `/goal status` to monitor progress on long-running "
"goals"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:46
msgid ""
"**Pause when needed**: `/goal pause` if you need the agent for something else"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:48
msgid "Self-Goaling (v0.3.61)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:50
msgid ""
"The agent can also set and drive its own multi-turn goals autonomously via "
"the `goal_manage` tool. This lets the agent break down a complex request "
"into self-directed goal loops without the user needing to invoke `/goal` "
"manually. The agent evaluates its own progress and adjusts course, the same "
"way a user-set `/goal` loop works."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:52
msgid "Availability"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:54
msgid ""
"`/goal` works across **all channels**: TUI, Telegram, Discord, Slack, and "
"WhatsApp. Set autonomous goals from wherever you talk to your agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:56
msgid "When to Use /goal vs /btw vs Plans"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:58
msgid "Use Case"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:60
msgid ""
"Autonomous loop for a single clear objective. Agent self-evaluates until "
"done."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:61
msgid "Spawn a parallel side task while you keep chatting."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:62
msgid ""
"Multi-step structured work with explicit tasks, dependencies, and acceptance "
"criteria."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/goal.md:64
msgid ""
"`/goal` is best when you have a clear outcome and want the agent to figure "
"out the steps itself."
msgstr ""

