#: src/features/web-scrape.md:3
msgid ""
"OpenCrabs includes a native URL-to-markdown scraping tool (`web_scrape`) "
"that converts any web page into clean markdown. Zero AI cost, zero API "
"tokens for the extraction itself. The agent uses `tool_search` to activate "
"it on demand, keeping it out of the always-loaded core tool set."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:7
msgid "`web_scrape` follows a five-step pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:9
msgid ""
"**Validate**: SSRF guard rejects private IPs, localhost, loopback, "
"link-local addresses, cloud metadata endpoints (169.254.169.254), and "
"non-http(s) schemes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:10
msgid ""
"**Fetch**: `reqwest` with browser User-Agent and timeout. `is_js_shell` "
"heuristic detects JS-heavy pages (React/Vue/Angular/Svelte shells, `<div "
"id=\"app\">`, no `<article>`). Escalates to browser manager when available"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:11
msgid ""
"**Extract**: CSS selector cascade (article, main, .content, etc.) isolates "
"primary content from HTML, falling back to body with junk selectors (header, "
"nav, sidebar, ads) removed"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:12
msgid ""
"**Clean**: Language-agnostic HTML cleaner strips scripts, styles, inline "
"handlers, HTML comments. Decodes entities, collapses blank lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:13
msgid ""
"**Convert**: `htmd` converts cleaned HTML to markdown. `absolutize_urls` "
"resolves relative src/href against page base URL. Images preserved as "
"`![alt](url)` tags for selective agent vision"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:15
msgid "Single URL Mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:17
msgid "Scrape a single URL and return the markdown content directly:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:19
msgid ""
"```\n"
"web_scrape https://example.com/page\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:23
msgid ""
"The agent receives the markdown in its context, ready for analysis, "
"summarisation, or extraction."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:25
msgid "Sitemap Mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:27
msgid "Discover and crawl an entire site via its sitemap:"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:29
msgid ""
"```\n"
"web_scrape https://example.com --sitemap\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:33
msgid ""
"This discovers `/sitemap.xml`, `/sitemap_index.xml`, and common variations. "
"Recursively crawls sitemap indexes (iterative worklist, 1000-URL cap, 3 "
"levels deep). Returns the URL list for the agent to pick from."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:35
msgid ""
"Each page's markdown is exported to a directory. The output path resolves to "
"the project files directory if the session is assigned to a project, or the "
"profile-scoped OpenCrabs home otherwise. Files never land outside managed "
"workspace."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:37
msgid ""
"**Pair it with memory:** point `[memory] extra_paths` at the export "
"directory and every scraped page becomes searchable via `memory_search "
"scope=\"external\"`, a zero-cost knowledge base your agent quotes verbatim. "
"Full walkthrough in [Memory System → Build a knowledge "
"base](../brain/memory.md#build-a-knowledge-base-from-any-docs-site). Note "
"the hard cap: 100 pages per sitemap scrape."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/web-scrape.md:39
msgid "SSRF Protection"
msgstr ""

