#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:17
msgid ""
"Some say that Flutter sucks… yeah (ironic) @opencrabs inside the phone "
"linked to a2a on a custom flutter app. It can change the OS. It can code "
"android app, compile and open it… all inside the freakin' phone"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:19
msgid ""
"First app fully built inside the phone using @opencrabs yes, code made "
"inside the phone, apk built and open. No need for a pc ;)"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:21
msgid ""
"**The device:** a Xiaomi Mi 8 (`dipper`), Android 10 / API 29, MIUI 12, "
"aarch64, kernel 4.9.186, 5.6 GB of RAM. Root came from the boot image "
"itself: Magisk patches it on the phone, fastboot flashes it, and a verifier "
"unpacks the result to inspect the ramdisk instead of trusting the patch log. "
"Live now: `magisk -c` reports `30.7:MAGISK:R`."
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:23
msgid ""
"**Getting a Linux userland onto Android took two attempts.** Generation one "
"shipped the `aarch64-linux-android` binary as a Magisk module with a "
"supervisor script, which meant a 59-file cfg port and a glibc-versus-musl "
"fight. Generation two, the one that runs today, is an Ubuntu 24.04.5 chroot "
"at glibc 2.39, which is what the released `linux-arm64` binary actually "
"wants. The trap that cost the most time: `/apex` is a tmpfs of per-apex bind "
"mounts, so a single bind of `/apex` copies an empty directory and every "
"Android binary dies with \"required file not found\", which reads like a "
"permission error but is a missing interpreter. The cure is binding each "
"`/apex/*` entry on its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:25
msgid ""
"**Then the app.** Daniel wanted the conversation UI he likes in the web, "
"built natively in Flutter, not a WebView. So the app speaks ACP (JSON-RPC "
"2.0 over stdio) to `opencrabs acp` running in the chroot, the same protocol "
"the TUI uses: live reasoning chunks, tool cards, permission prompts, token "
"usage. No browser, no server, no open port."
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:27
msgid ""
"**Survives a reboot with nobody touching the phone:** a JobScheduler job "
"that re-arms itself unconditionally, a service hook that waits for "
"`sys.boot_completed` and re-establishes the seven mounts, and a loop that "
"reapplies MIUI's idle and autostart appops because the powerkeeper clears "
"the battery exemption about 20 s after boot"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:28
msgid ""
"**Proof, from logcat after a real reboot:** handshake ok at 12 s, service "
"up, battery exemption settled, then a headless self test of **12 pass / 0 "
"fail, GREEN** in 3.7 s covering the binary version, shell, sessions, boot "
"wiring, service state, battery exemption, voice recognizer, mic permission, "
"widget binding, ACP ready and a real prompt"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:29
msgid ""
"**The APK built on the phone:** MIUI ships its screen-recorder tile with "
"only a 20 KB stub behind it, so tapping it opens the app store and records "
"nothing. The crab wrote a real Quick Settings tile, built it in six steps "
"with no Gradle and no SDK manager, and put it in the panel next to WiFi. "
"**12,784 bytes.**"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:30
msgid ""
"**The build chain:** `aapt2 compile` → `aapt2 link` → `javac --release 8` "
"against `android.jar` → `d8` from R8 → zip the dex in → `zipalign` → "
"`apksigner sign` and `verify`"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:31
msgid ""
"**Installed from inside the chroot**, reaching Android's package manager "
"through `nsenter -t 1 -m`, then granted root by writing a Magisk policy row "
"and added to the shade with `cmd statusbar add-tile`"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:32
msgid ""
"**One body, two brains:** ACP is stdio and `ssh -T` is also stdio, so the "
"phone can point at a Mac on the LAN with no bridge and no open port. "
"Measured: `initialize` in 1.2 s, remote session list of 40, self test 9/9 "
"GREEN against the remote brain"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:34
msgid ""
"**The part that matters:** the tile does not record anything itself. It "
"shells out, through Magisk's `su`, to the same recorder binary in the chroot "
"that the `/rec` chat command uses, so there is one recorder, one state file, "
"one output folder. The crab wrote an Android app that is a **handle for a "
"Linux tool inside the same phone**. The app is the thumb, the crab is the "
"brain. That is the whole architecture of this project, in 13 KB."
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-crab-lives-inside-the-phone.md:36
msgid ""
"The reasoning log from that session is the detail worth keeping: the crab "
"stopped to check whether it was really on a phone, and confirmed it from the "
"runtime instead of assuming."
msgstr ""

