#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:5
msgid "_GitHub · Family_ **Research**"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:17
msgid ""
"Check the Tbilisi airport website: tomorrow's Azimuth flight to Moscow "
"Vnukovo, around 14:00, has it been rescheduled?"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:19
msgid ""
"A one-line question with real consequences. The butler treated it like an "
"ops incident:"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:21
msgid ""
"**Airline ops feed, scraped:** the schedule page embeds live ops data as "
"JSON inside the HTML; the agent extracted and parsed it (186 flights, 4-day "
"window, planned/actual times and statuses)"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:22
msgid ""
"**Airport live board, reverse-engineered:** the departure board loads from "
"an undocumented AJAX endpoint; the agent read the page's own JS to find the "
"correct parameter and got structured JSON back (scheduled/estimated/actual "
"times, remarks, gates)"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:23
msgid ""
"**A hypothesis, then the kill shot:** the flight was missing from tomorrow's "
"board while a partner-coded flight held the same slot, codeshare, right? "
"Flight history said no: both numbers departed the same day ~20 minutes "
"apart, two separate physical aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:24
msgid ""
"**Rotation check:** the inbound positioning leg for tomorrow was missing "
"from the ops feed too, closing the loop"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:25
msgid ""
"**The honest verdict:** not delayed, not rescheduled, dropped from that date "
"entirely. Alternatives named, and \"I don't know the reason, the airline "
"hasn't published one\" said plainly instead of guessed"
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:27
msgid ""
"The same profile, the same day: dose-frequency health questions answered "
"against peer-reviewed sources with proper caveats and red-flag lists, a "
"forwarded astronomy fun-fact corrected with dry humor (the distance ratio is "
"~389×, not 400×, close enough for folklore, not for a butler), and a "
"contested science question answered citing studies on both sides."
msgstr ""

#: src/stories/the-butler-that-overturned-its-own-hypothesis.md:29
msgid ""
"[Full write-up (issue #27) "
"↗](https://github.com/adolfousier/opencrabs.com/issues/27)"
msgstr ""

