"thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:120
msgid "Session correlation (#1078)"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:122
msgid ""
"Every agent turn opens a `tracing` span carrying its `session_id`, so each "
"log line emitted inside that turn is stamped with it. Cron jobs open a `job` "
"span (name + id) and the RSI engine opens its own. Spawned tasks inherit the "
"span, so work that moves onto another task still reports the turn it belongs "
"to."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:124
msgid ""
"This makes a single turn greppable out of a file where every session, cron "
"job and RSI cycle is interleaved:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:127
msgid "'<session-id>'"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:130
msgid ""
"Before this, filtering was guesswork: thread ids get reused and outlive a "
"turn, and timestamps only narrow the window."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:132
msgid "Writer reliability (#1115, #1077)"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:134
msgid ""
"The file writer is deliberately synchronous rather than using a background "
"worker, because the worker swallows IO errors and drops events under load. "
"Two failure modes were fixed in v0.3.82:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:136
msgid ""
"**Events were dropped, and log output could reach the TUI's terminal** "
"(#1115), corrupting the display."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/architecture.md:137
msgid ""
"**A stalled write silenced everything** (#1077). The writer held a mutex for "
"the duration of a write, so if one write blocked (a hung filesystem, disk "
"pressure), every other thread trying to log blocked behind it. One parked "
"write could take the whole process's logging down while the agent kept "
"running. The writer now uses `try_lock`: under contention the event is "
"dropped rather than blocking the caller, so one stalled write can never "
"silence another thread."
msgstr ""

