#: src/development/security.md:79
msgid "Safety Gates (v0.3.78)"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:81
msgid "OpenCrabs v0.3.78 introduced a layered safety-gate system:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:83
msgid "TOML Bash Blocklist"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:84
msgid ""
"Shell commands are checked against a TOML-defined blocklist before "
"execution. Dangerous patterns (recursive deletes on root, raw disk writes, "
"fork bombs) are rejected with a clear error. The blocklist is "
"user-extensible and hot-reloads on file change. See "
"[Configuration](../getting-started/configuration.md#toml-bash-blocklist-v0378) "
"for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:86
msgid "Secret Redaction"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:87
msgid ""
"Quoted secrets in agent output are now **redacted before delivery**. This "
"covers:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:88
msgid "Bearer tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:89
msgid "API key patterns"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:90
msgid "Colon-token shapes (key: value in YAML-like output)"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:91
msgid "Query-param keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:92
msgid "URL passwords"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:94
msgid ""
"Redaction fires on all delivery paths (TUI, Telegram, Discord, Slack, "
"WhatsApp), so a secret accidentally echoed by the agent never reaches the "
"chat."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:96
msgid "Brain File Verification"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:97
msgid ""
"Post-write verification (via brain_verify.toml) ensures brain files maintain "
"their structural integrity after RSI writes. Required anchors (H1 title, "
"Owns header) are checked, and writes that break structure are flagged."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:99
msgid "Harness-Level Denials (v0.5.1)"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:101
msgid ""
"Prompt instructions are a request; the harness is a wall. The v0.5.1 "
"hardening batch moved the load-bearing safety rules out of brain-file prose "
"and into code paths that run even when the model is jailbroken or an RSI "
"pass weakens a prompt file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:105
msgid ""
"**Confidential-path deny on `read_file`**: resolved paths matching the "
"agent's own `keys.toml`, anything under a `.ssh/` directory, SSH private-key "
"names, `.env` files, `.pem` / `.key` / `.pfx` material, `/etc/shadow`, or "
"files that name themselves a credential are refused **before a byte is "
"read**. Public keys and ordinary files are unaffected, and `..`/`~` spelling "
"does not change the verdict."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:110
msgid ""
"**One SSRF guard for every fetch tool**: `web_scrape` and `http_request` "
"share `brain::tools::ssrf`: cloud metadata endpoints (by name as well as "
"IP), RFC1918/LAN, IPv6 link-local, the unspecified addresses, CGNAT "
"`100.64.0.0/10`, and IPv4-mapped IPv6 forms are blocked; domains are "
"DNS-resolved and **every** answer checked before the request, and each "
"redirect hop is re-validated, so a public-looking name or a 302 cannot "
"smuggle an internal target. Loopback stays deliberately allowed: a "
"local-first agent legitimately reaches the operator's own machine."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:117
msgid ""
"**The bash blocklist floor everywhere**: `execute_code` and dynamic shell "
"tools now pass through the same blocklist as `bash` (hardcoded plus the user "
"TOML list), checked before writing or running, for every language, since "
"`os.system`/`subprocess` can carry the same command. Dynamic tools also "
"cannot be named like core tools: `add_tool` refuses to create an unguarded "
"stand-in for `bash`, `read_file`, `evolve`, and friends."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:122
msgid ""
"**Deny-by-default channel allowlists**: an unconfigured Discord or Slack "
"channel now refuses everyone (matching Telegram): empty "
"`allowed_users`/`allowed_roles` is no longer \"accept all\". On WhatsApp an "
"empty `allowed_phones` no longer elevates strangers to owner. Details per "
"channel in [Channels overview](../channels/overview.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:126
msgid ""
"**Verified self-update**: `/evolve` checks the release `SHA256SUMS` against "
"the download before swapping the binary, and the download host is pinned, so "
"a redirected release asset cannot hot-swap an unverified binary."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/security.md:130
msgid ""
"These complement the v0.3.78 safety gates above; together they mean a "
"stranger who reaches a channel, or a prompt injection that reaches a tool, "
"meets code that refuses, not prose that asks politely."
msgstr ""

